1
00:00:17,633 --> 00:00:19,000
Game. I'm ready, Director.

2
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:25,967
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

3
00:00:28,167 --> 00:00:29,367
[STAFF] Five! Four!

4
00:00:29,367 --> 00:00:31,367
[VICE] Oh, wait a second.
Let's pray first.

5
00:00:31,367 --> 00:00:33,100
Let's ask for a blessing first.

6
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:34,267
In the name of the Father,
of the Son,

7
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:36,300
and of the Holy Spirit,
Amen.

8
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:39,033
Lord God, thank you so much
for this day.

9
00:00:39,033 --> 00:00:42,600
Thank you so much for letting us
stay in your world,

10
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:44,400
and for blessing us so much.

11
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:48,800
Thank you, Lord, for giving us
so many opportunities.

12
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:52,600
An opportunity to receive
your blessings.

13
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:56,700
An opportunity to give
and receive love.

14
00:00:56,700 --> 00:01:01,500
An opportunity to use
the talent you've granted us.

15
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:03,500
An opportunity to work.

16
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:06,700
An opportunity to entertain
our viewers.

17
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:11,500
An opportunity to serve

18
00:01:11,533 --> 00:01:14,233
to our colleagues.

19
00:01:14,233 --> 00:01:19,000
An opportunity for us all
to meet and have fun.

20
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:22,000
An opportunity to make
content with our program

21
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,467
that aims to bring happiness to
many Filipinos around the world.

22
00:01:25,467 --> 00:01:28,267
And thank you very much,
Lord Jesus Christ.

23
00:01:28,267 --> 00:01:30,067
We know you'll guide us
all the way

24
00:01:30,067 --> 00:01:31,867
from the beginning until
the end of our program.

25
00:01:31,867 --> 00:01:36,067
Fill our studio
with laughter, positivity,

26
00:01:36,067 --> 00:01:39,067
happiness, and liveliness.

27
00:01:39,067 --> 00:01:41,867
We pray that we'll always
have a smile on our faces.

28
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:45,700
We pray that we start and
end the show filled with joy.

29
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:49,900
We also pray that our guests
and everyone here with us

30
00:01:49,900 --> 00:01:52,100
will have a great time here

31
00:01:52,100 --> 00:01:54,800
so they can have stories to tell
people when they return home.

32
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:58,400
We hope that we can create
some wonderful core memories

33
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:03,200
that we will carry with us
even when time passes by.

34
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:05,500
Thank you very much,
Lord Jesus Christ.

35
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:09,700
The success and glory
of our show is all yours.

36
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:10,900
Thank you very much.

37
00:02:10,900 --> 00:02:13,300
We know that
this episode will be great.

38
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:15,600
In Jesus' name we pray,
Amen.

39
00:02:15,633 --> 00:02:16,833
In the name of the Father,
of the Son,

40
00:02:16,833 --> 00:02:18,767
and of the Holy Spirit,
Amen.

41
00:02:18,767 --> 00:02:20,567
Let's go!

42
00:02:20,567 --> 00:02:23,767
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

43
00:02:23,767 --> 00:02:27,000
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

44
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:29,133
Ah, that's all right.

45
00:02:29,333 --> 00:02:30,467
Okay.

46
00:02:30,467 --> 00:02:33,000
Okay, so I will enter again
from the door,

47
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
and then pretend like
it's your first time seeing me.

48
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,167
- [AUDIENCE SQUEALING]
- Is that all right?

49
00:02:37,167 --> 00:02:39,000
So just act like that.

50
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:43,767
Act like for the first time
in six years,

51
00:02:43,767 --> 00:02:45,267
we've finally seen
each other again.

52
00:02:45,267 --> 00:02:46,467
Is that okay?

53
00:02:46,467 --> 00:02:48,000
- [AUDIENCE SHOUTING] Yes!
- Okay.

54
00:02:48,033 --> 00:02:51,467
And when you see me,
act like you really love me.

55
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:53,700
Act as if you don't see
anything wrong

56
00:02:53,700 --> 00:02:55,700
with everything I do on TV.

57
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:58,867
Act like you fully accept
all of me, you know.

58
00:02:59,067 --> 00:03:00,600
So we're just going
to fool ourselves a little bit.

59
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:01,767
[VICE] Let's go.

60
00:03:02,300 --> 00:03:04,467
Come on, my feet
are hurting already.

61
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:06,467
[STAFF] Hold it!

62
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:13,300
[VICE] First...

63
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:14,767
Wait a minute.

64
00:03:19,733 --> 00:03:21,933
[VICE] Okay, I'm ready.

65
00:03:22,267 --> 00:03:26,467
[STAFF] Five! Four!
Three! Two! One!

66
00:03:26,467 --> 00:03:33,433
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

67
00:03:34,467 --> 00:03:36,467
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

68
00:03:36,467 --> 00:03:38,667
Yes!

69
00:03:38,667 --> 00:03:44,467
<i> Gandang Gabi,
Kapamilya</i> and Kapuso!

70
00:03:44,467 --> 00:03:46,667
[AUDIENCE] Gandang Gabi Vice!

71
00:03:46,667 --> 00:03:49,867
[VICE] Oh my god!
I missed that greeting!

72
00:03:49,867 --> 00:03:52,367
<i> Gandang Gabi!</i>

73
00:03:52,367 --> 00:03:54,567
<i> Gandang Gabi!</i>

74
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:56,400
Good evening!

75
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:58,800
Good evening to all of you!

76
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:00,800
I missed you!

77
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:01,800
I...

78
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:03,033
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

79
00:04:03,033 --> 00:04:05,767
I think you were also here
the last time we were here.

80
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:08,700
- So you're all still alive!
- [LAUGHTER SFX]

81
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:10,400
How fantastic!

82
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:14,200
[VICE] None of you were beaten
by the pandemic!

83
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:17,033
- You're all still here. Yes!
- [AUDIENCE SQUEALING]

84
00:04:17,033 --> 00:04:20,433
But I think my Little Ponies
got a bit chubbier.

85
00:04:20,433 --> 00:04:24,633
Oh my god, I'm so happy!

86
00:04:24,633 --> 00:04:26,033
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

87
00:04:26,033 --> 00:04:28,000
Here we go!

88
00:04:29,167 --> 00:04:31,000
We've finally seen
each other again.

89
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,000
We're all together again
every Sunday night

90
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,767
on Gandang Gabi Vice!

91
00:04:35,767 --> 00:04:37,000
[CHEERING]

92
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,467
[VICE] I'm so happy.
Are you so happy?

93
00:04:39,467 --> 00:04:40,667
[AUDIENCE] Yes!

94
00:04:40,667 --> 00:04:42,167
Are you excited?

95
00:04:42,167 --> 00:04:43,367
[AUDIENCE] Yes!

96
00:04:43,367 --> 00:04:45,567
My gosh! Did you miss GGV?

97
00:04:45,567 --> 00:04:46,767
[AUDIENCE] Yes!

98
00:04:46,767 --> 00:04:49,967
Wow! I feel so happy.

99
00:04:50,267 --> 00:04:53,767
I missed this so much and
I also missed you all so much.

100
00:04:53,767 --> 00:04:55,000
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

101
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:58,433
I missed all the hijinks
we used to do here.

102
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:00,167
I missed the episodes when

103
00:05:00,167 --> 00:05:02,667
we had more bleeps
than scenes aired.

104
00:05:02,700 --> 00:05:06,900
I missed
our controversial episodes!

105
00:05:06,900 --> 00:05:10,700
We're going to make
more of those now!

106
00:05:10,700 --> 00:05:13,700
We're going back
to our messy antics!

107
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:14,900
[LAUGHTER SFX]

108
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:16,700
How fun. I missed you all.

109
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:17,800
Group hug.

110
00:05:18,967 --> 00:05:20,100
Group hug.

111
00:05:21,133 --> 00:05:22,300
Group hug.

112
00:05:22,967 --> 00:05:24,967
Wow, look at the audience
in the middle.

113
00:05:24,967 --> 00:05:27,967
They look like
they're the board of judges,

114
00:05:27,967 --> 00:05:30,967
here to judge us today.

115
00:05:30,967 --> 00:05:34,733
[CHUCKLES] They look like
representatives sent by MTRCB.

116
00:05:34,767 --> 00:05:38,267
They look like they were sent by
the management, the advertisers,

117
00:05:38,267 --> 00:05:40,100
and the suppliers from
our last season

118
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:41,867
who haven't been paid yet.

119
00:05:41,867 --> 00:05:42,867
- [LAUGHTER SFX]
- They're all here.

120
00:05:42,867 --> 00:05:45,067
[VICE] But let's come
and talk to them.

121
00:05:45,267 --> 00:05:47,667
There. Let's go here.

122
00:05:47,667 --> 00:05:49,467
Hi, sir! Gandang Gabi!

123
00:05:49,467 --> 00:05:50,467
<i> Gandang Gabi Vice!</i>

124
00:05:50,467 --> 00:05:52,467
- What's your name?
- Jason.

125
00:05:52,467 --> 00:05:54,667
[VICE] Jason, can you
please stand up?

126
00:05:54,667 --> 00:05:56,667
Please stand up for
just a second.

127
00:05:56,667 --> 00:05:58,867
Ah, you're already standing.
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

128
00:05:58,867 --> 00:06:00,867
- Sir!
- [LAUGHTER SFX]

129
00:06:00,867 --> 00:06:04,367
This is the new season of<i> GGV
</i>on GMA.

130
00:06:04,367 --> 00:06:08,167
Have you really watched<i> GGV
</i>from our first seasons?

131
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:10,700
Yes, I also watched the uncut
versions on YouTube.

132
00:06:10,700 --> 00:06:12,900
Oh, really?
You like things that are uncut?

133
00:06:12,900 --> 00:06:14,067
Yes.

134
00:06:14,067 --> 00:06:16,500
I'm personally not a big fan
of things that are uncut.

135
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:19,533
I prefer the edited versions.

136
00:06:19,533 --> 00:06:20,767
Just kidding. Okay.

137
00:06:20,767 --> 00:06:25,733
What's your favorite or
most memorable episode of GGV

138
00:06:25,733 --> 00:06:27,333
that you've watched?

139
00:06:27,333 --> 00:06:29,133
The reunion episode of
<i> Palibhasa Lalake.</i>

140
00:06:29,133 --> 00:06:33,533
Ah! The one with Richard Gomez,
Joey Marquez, and John Estrada.

141
00:06:33,533 --> 00:06:37,333
When they revealed
who was dating who.

142
00:06:37,333 --> 00:06:39,133
Yes! How fun.

143
00:06:39,133 --> 00:06:44,133
So you like it when our guests
are from the 90s and 80s, right?

144
00:06:44,167 --> 00:06:45,467
- Yes, yes.
- Really?

145
00:06:45,467 --> 00:06:48,000
So what are you looking forward
to watch this time?

146
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,267
Well, you have
a wider reach now.

147
00:06:50,267 --> 00:06:53,100
You can have both<i> Kapuso
and Kapamilya</i> guests.

148
00:06:53,100 --> 00:06:56,567
So you will be able
to invite more people now.

149
00:06:56,567 --> 00:07:00,000
Not only is my reach wider now,
I'm looser now too.

150
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,367
- [LAUGHTER SFX]
- Right.

151
00:07:01,367 --> 00:07:04,367
Of course, that's because
we can afford loose change now.

152
00:07:04,367 --> 00:07:05,767
Don't be green-minded.

153
00:07:05,767 --> 00:07:11,667
But I'm also excited to be with
people I haven't interviewed yet

154
00:07:11,667 --> 00:07:13,000
from GMA.

155
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:16,867
Because I guess
99% of our guests

156
00:07:16,900 --> 00:07:19,633
have come from ABS-CBN, right?

157
00:07:19,633 --> 00:07:23,433
But we are freer now,
so we can talk to more people!

158
00:07:23,433 --> 00:07:25,433
- [AUDIENCE CHEERING]
- Yes!

159
00:07:25,433 --> 00:07:30,433
Which GMA artist would you like
to see me chat with?

160
00:07:30,433 --> 00:07:32,633
- Dingdong Dantes.
- Ah, Dingdong Dantes.

161
00:07:32,633 --> 00:07:35,333
But he's been a guest
on<i> GGV</i> twice already.

162
00:07:35,333 --> 00:07:37,333
Where were you when
we aired those episodes?

163
00:07:37,333 --> 00:07:38,533
- [LAUGHTER SFX]
- Sorry, sorry.

164
00:07:38,533 --> 00:07:40,067
So you don't always
watch<i> GGV</i> then.

165
00:07:40,067 --> 00:07:41,533
I don't want to talk
to you anymore.

166
00:07:41,533 --> 00:07:43,533
You only watch sometimes.

167
00:07:43,533 --> 00:07:46,067
Are you one of those people
who only watch us sometimes,

168
00:07:46,067 --> 00:07:47,100
but still bash us?

169
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:49,433
- No, I'm not!
- Oh, you're not one of them.

170
00:07:49,467 --> 00:07:51,167
But thank you very much.
What brought you here?

171
00:07:51,167 --> 00:07:52,567
Does the production team
owe you money?

172
00:07:52,567 --> 00:07:53,767
- No.
- Oh, none?

173
00:07:53,767 --> 00:07:55,767
So you just want to experience

174
00:07:55,767 --> 00:07:59,000
the first episode of
the new season of GGV?

175
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,133
- Yes.
- Thank you very much.

176
00:08:01,667 --> 00:08:03,433
Yes!

177
00:08:04,567 --> 00:08:08,367
And as you can see,
since we have a new season,

178
00:08:08,367 --> 00:08:10,533
we have a new home!

179
00:08:11,267 --> 00:08:14,567
We've exhausted
our previous home already.

180
00:08:14,567 --> 00:08:18,033
It's gone through
a lot of trials.

181
00:08:18,033 --> 00:08:21,500
Disaster, rain, typhoons,
floods, and earthquakes.

182
00:08:21,533 --> 00:08:22,533
It's been haunted
with ghosts too.

183
00:08:22,533 --> 00:08:25,300
So now, we have
a brand new home.

184
00:08:26,433 --> 00:08:28,967
And since it's very new,
I've invited some people over.

185
00:08:28,967 --> 00:08:32,967
I invited you all to come over
into my new home,

186
00:08:32,967 --> 00:08:36,933
and to join me
in my house blessing.

187
00:08:37,233 --> 00:08:41,233
But I'm sorry because
I was too busy preparing myself,

188
00:08:41,233 --> 00:08:43,733
so I forgot to prepare
my house properly.

189
00:08:43,733 --> 00:08:47,733
So as you can see,
this was just delivered here.

190
00:08:47,733 --> 00:08:49,833
We had a hard time looking
for a sponsor who would

191
00:08:49,833 --> 00:08:51,967
accept payment in installments
for 12 years.

192
00:08:51,967 --> 00:08:54,133
You know what the industry
is going through right now,

193
00:08:54,133 --> 00:08:56,967
so we can't pay in one go,
you know.

194
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:00,000
This was just delivered,
so I hadn't prepared it yet.

195
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:03,567
I did my makeup first and
focused on how I looked

196
00:09:03,567 --> 00:09:06,767
because I can't greet guests
without looking pretty, right?

197
00:09:06,767 --> 00:09:08,533
But...

198
00:09:08,867 --> 00:09:11,100
I looked beautiful when
you all came over, right?

199
00:09:11,100 --> 00:09:18,000
["ANGEL BABY" BY
TROYE SIVAN PLAYING]

200
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:24,033
- [LAUGHTER SFX]
- That's how you do it.

201
00:09:24,033 --> 00:09:27,500
[VICE] I look like an idiot
on the logo again, don't I?

202
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:28,700
You've missed that too,
haven't you?

203
00:09:28,733 --> 00:09:30,967
The way I look like
I'm falling over.

204
00:09:30,967 --> 00:09:33,733
It seems like I look younger,
don't I?

205
00:09:33,733 --> 00:09:34,933
[AUDIENCE] Yes!

206
00:09:34,933 --> 00:09:38,833
Of course, celebrities like
to age backwards nowadays.

207
00:09:38,833 --> 00:09:40,833
We like to look as if
we're getting younger.

208
00:09:40,833 --> 00:09:42,633
But since my house is brand new,

209
00:09:42,633 --> 00:09:45,433
I don't want to feel lonely,
of course.

210
00:09:45,433 --> 00:09:48,233
I'm done with my era of
being lonely and alone.

211
00:09:48,233 --> 00:09:49,233
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

212
00:09:49,233 --> 00:09:51,067
I'm more used to being
with people now.

213
00:09:51,067 --> 00:09:55,067
So in my new home, I'll be
joined with new housemates.

214
00:09:55,067 --> 00:09:58,500
They will also be with you
every Sunday aside from me.

215
00:09:58,700 --> 00:10:00,633
Where are they?

216
00:10:00,633 --> 00:10:02,967
I already told them that
we have a house blessing.

217
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:04,767
Why are they still not here?
I even arrived before them.

218
00:10:04,767 --> 00:10:06,100
But they were
already here earlier.

219
00:10:06,100 --> 00:10:07,567
They received the delivery.

220
00:10:07,567 --> 00:10:09,367
Tetay! Verna!

221
00:10:09,367 --> 00:10:10,567
[VICE SQUEALS]

222
00:10:10,567 --> 00:10:13,100
- [TETAY WHOOPING]
<i> - Gandang Gabi Vice!</i>

223
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:15,100
<i> Gandang Gabi Vice!</i>

224
00:10:15,100 --> 00:10:16,867
[VICE] Hey! Where have you been?

225
00:10:16,867 --> 00:10:18,667
Our visitors are already here.

226
00:10:18,667 --> 00:10:21,467
We'll call you again later
when we need you.

227
00:10:21,467 --> 00:10:23,467
I'm also one of
your partners here, Meme!

228
00:10:23,467 --> 00:10:24,967
My gosh, I already said that...

229
00:10:25,167 --> 00:10:28,167
I already told you to receive
the furniture I had delivered.

230
00:10:28,167 --> 00:10:30,367
I didn't ask you to buy
a propane tank.

231
00:10:30,367 --> 00:10:33,167
I was doing the laundry earlier,
so I just picked this up too.

232
00:10:33,167 --> 00:10:35,167
But wait a minute,
let's greet them first.

233
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:36,600
One, two, three.

234
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:39,800
[IN UNISON] Gandang Gabi Vice!

235
00:10:39,800 --> 00:10:41,000
Yes!

236
00:10:41,300 --> 00:10:43,800
They will be my new housemates
in our new home.

237
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:46,800
- Meet Tetay and Verna. Yes.
- Hello!

238
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:50,300
You've already seen Verna on
Breaking Muse on It's Showtime.

239
00:10:50,300 --> 00:10:53,033
You've also seen Tetay
tag along with us sometimes.

240
00:10:53,033 --> 00:10:55,500
He vlogs and he also appears
on<i> It's Showtime</i> sometimes,

241
00:10:55,500 --> 00:10:58,800
as well as on other programs
on GMA and ABS-CBN.

242
00:10:58,800 --> 00:11:01,033
- You really came prepared, huh?
- Of course!

243
00:11:01,033 --> 00:11:03,500
- You came too ready.
- Well, look at yourself.

244
00:11:03,500 --> 00:11:04,900
I prepared for this, Meme.

245
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:07,400
For the first time, I think
a mandarin might be bitter.

246
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:08,400
[VERNA CHUCKLES]

247
00:11:08,433 --> 00:11:11,233
Usually, a mandarin
tastes sweet,

248
00:11:11,233 --> 00:11:12,433
but this one looks bitter!

249
00:11:12,433 --> 00:11:14,233
- This is not a mandarin, Meme.
- So what is it?

250
00:11:14,233 --> 00:11:15,433
This is Sharmaine.

251
00:11:15,433 --> 00:11:17,567
- Oh, you've changed.
- Yes.

252
00:11:17,567 --> 00:11:20,000
So you've changed your name.
You should've changed faces too.

253
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:21,667
- My gosh!
- [VERNA AND TETAY CHUCKLE]

254
00:11:21,667 --> 00:11:24,867
If a papaya soap is like this,
I don't want to use it anymore.

255
00:11:24,867 --> 00:11:27,367
If she was a papaya soap,
would you use it?

256
00:11:27,367 --> 00:11:29,367
- Well, I'm beautiful.
- Her figure's like a papaya.

257
00:11:29,367 --> 00:11:30,867
But isn't her face like
that of a sapodilla?

258
00:11:30,867 --> 00:11:32,367
[LAUGHING]

259
00:11:32,367 --> 00:11:34,167
[VICE] But we have
a house blessing tonight.

260
00:11:34,167 --> 00:11:36,667
How could we bless our home
if you did not prepare?

261
00:11:36,667 --> 00:11:38,867
We brought some stuff!

262
00:11:38,867 --> 00:11:40,867
I brought sugar.

263
00:11:40,900 --> 00:11:43,133
[VICE] Right, we need sugar
in our new home

264
00:11:43,133 --> 00:11:48,600
because it will bring good luck
and levity in our home.

265
00:11:48,600 --> 00:11:50,800
- Ayan.
- [TETAY] We have sugar, rice...

266
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:52,300
- Okay, rice!
- We also have salt.

267
00:11:52,300 --> 00:11:54,300
[VICE] We need to have rice
and salt as we enter the house.

268
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:56,500
- There we go.
- It's all in there.

269
00:11:56,500 --> 00:11:58,500
And of course,
we also have coins!

270
00:11:58,500 --> 00:12:01,033
- [TETAY AND VERNA] Yes!
- [AUDIENCE CHEERING]

271
00:12:01,033 --> 00:12:03,500
[TETAY] Catch them
for good luck!

272
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:04,700
We have coins.

273
00:12:04,700 --> 00:12:07,200
- Whoo!
- And, of course, the coins...

274
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:09,033
can be donated to our neighbors

275
00:12:09,033 --> 00:12:12,033
- or you can catch them!
- Hey! [LAUGHS]

276
00:12:12,033 --> 00:12:13,500
That will hurt, Meme!

277
00:12:13,500 --> 00:12:17,433
Some neighbors just attend
house blessings to catch coins.

278
00:12:17,467 --> 00:12:18,467
- [LAUGHING]
- [AUDIENCE CHEERING]

279
00:12:18,467 --> 00:12:20,667
How was your throw like?

280
00:12:20,667 --> 00:12:21,867
Yes! See that?

281
00:12:21,867 --> 00:12:24,667
It's like you're shooting
using a bamboo gun.

282
00:12:24,667 --> 00:12:27,167
- Just like that.
- Hey, catch it for good luck!

283
00:12:27,167 --> 00:12:29,667
It's good luck
but wait a minute!

284
00:12:29,667 --> 00:12:31,467
How embarrassing.
Our neighbors are already here.

285
00:12:31,467 --> 00:12:33,267
But you haven't fixed up
the furniture yet.

286
00:12:33,267 --> 00:12:35,267
Fix up the furniture!

287
00:12:35,267 --> 00:12:37,433
These brats!

288
00:12:37,633 --> 00:12:40,100
[TETAY] Let's just be grateful
that we even have furniture.

289
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:41,867
[VICE] Why did you even
have to wear that?

290
00:12:41,867 --> 00:12:43,867
- Don't you have a uniform here?
- [AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

291
00:12:43,867 --> 00:12:45,667
Girl, I might just return you
to your agency.

292
00:12:45,667 --> 00:12:47,133
You should be thankful
because...

293
00:12:47,333 --> 00:12:49,767
you're the only one we hired
from the Stinky Agency.

294
00:12:49,800 --> 00:12:51,267
[COMICAL SFX]

295
00:12:52,033 --> 00:12:54,033
- Let's fix this up.
- What should we do?

296
00:12:54,033 --> 00:12:55,200
[BUBBLE WRAP POPPING]

297
00:12:55,200 --> 00:12:57,400
- She's not a garbage bag!
- Oh, sorry.

298
00:12:57,400 --> 00:12:58,900
Oh, you look beautiful
like that.

299
00:12:58,900 --> 00:13:01,900
- [UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]
- Oh! Oh! Oh! Oh!

300
00:13:01,900 --> 00:13:04,133
Oh, it's Lotus Feet!

301
00:13:04,133 --> 00:13:05,300
[LAUGHTER SFX]

302
00:13:05,300 --> 00:13:07,100
[VICE] And where should
we put this?

303
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:11,200
There, perfect!

304
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:12,900
Fix those up.
It's embarrassing.

305
00:13:12,900 --> 00:13:15,367
I didn't know that it's just
easy to arrange furniture.

306
00:13:15,567 --> 00:13:18,633
Furnitures in new homes
should be well-arranged.

307
00:13:18,633 --> 00:13:20,633
Some people even hire interior
designers for their homes.

308
00:13:20,633 --> 00:13:22,133
But we're doing it ourselves.

309
00:13:22,167 --> 00:13:24,167
Well, you just need
to push things around.

310
00:13:24,167 --> 00:13:25,633
- There we go.
- Okay.

311
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,967
There we go.

312
00:13:28,267 --> 00:13:30,267
We're all done now.

313
00:13:30,267 --> 00:13:32,067
[TETAY] Yehey!

314
00:13:32,367 --> 00:13:34,867
But we don't have
any guests yet.

315
00:13:34,867 --> 00:13:36,867
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

316
00:13:36,867 --> 00:13:39,367
Our efforts would go to waste
if we wouldn't have any guests.

317
00:13:39,367 --> 00:13:41,167
[TETAY] Would you be all right
if we had no guests?

318
00:13:41,167 --> 00:13:43,000
[VICE YELPS]
We cannot have no guests.

319
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:45,000
- You startled me.
- Yeah.

320
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,467
It seems like you've had
a lot of coffee, huh?

321
00:13:46,467 --> 00:13:48,267
- What a clumsy gay man.
- Yes.

322
00:13:48,267 --> 00:13:50,267
Of course, we can't have
no guests around.

323
00:13:50,267 --> 00:13:56,767
Our<i> Kapamilya</i> and<i> Kapuso</i> viewers
waited so long for this.

324
00:13:56,800 --> 00:13:58,100
Of course,
we can't let that happen.

325
00:13:58,100 --> 00:14:04,200
We cannot let our first episode
not have an explosive guest.

326
00:14:04,200 --> 00:14:05,400
[TETAY] That's right.

327
00:14:05,400 --> 00:14:06,900
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

328
00:14:06,900 --> 00:14:08,367
Since we're on GMA now...

329
00:14:08,900 --> 00:14:11,400
our first guest has
to be a Kapuso.

330
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:13,200
[AUDIENCE SQUEALING, CHEERING]

331
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:16,033
[TETAY] Our neighbors
seem very excited.

332
00:14:16,033 --> 00:14:18,433
You haven't said a thing yet
but they're already screaming.

333
00:14:18,433 --> 00:14:20,967
- Who could it be?
- Where's my phone?

334
00:14:20,967 --> 00:14:22,700
[VICE] I'm going
to pick a guest...

335
00:14:23,133 --> 00:14:26,633
from my contact list who
I can call over here.

336
00:14:26,633 --> 00:14:28,433
[YELPS] Someone texted me.

337
00:14:28,467 --> 00:14:31,000
- You haven't called one yet?
- Someone texted me.

338
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:34,000
- NDRRMC. Oh gosh!
- [LAUGHTER SFX]

339
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:36,000
I always feel worried when
I receive their text.

340
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:39,967
Okay, which<i> Kapuso</i> in my contact
list seems fun to talk to?

341
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,467
Oh, here it is!

342
00:14:42,467 --> 00:14:44,267
[GASPS] Oh!

343
00:14:44,267 --> 00:14:45,467
[VERNA] Oh!

344
00:14:45,467 --> 00:14:48,467
Let's call him first.

345
00:14:48,467 --> 00:14:50,567
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

346
00:14:50,567 --> 00:14:51,767
He doesn't seem
to have mobile data.

347
00:14:51,767 --> 00:14:53,267
[VERNA CHUCKLES]

348
00:14:53,267 --> 00:14:54,433
Hello?

349
00:14:55,267 --> 00:14:56,733
Please come here.

350
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:58,433
I want to talk to you.

351
00:14:58,633 --> 00:15:00,733
- [VERNA] Oh my.
- [TETAY] Is that your guest?

352
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,000
[ALDEN] Hello? Hello?

353
00:15:02,033 --> 00:15:03,033
[AUDIENCE SQUEALING, CHEERING]

354
00:15:03,033 --> 00:15:04,467
[ALDEN] Hello, guys.

355
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:06,900
Wait a minute.

356
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:08,700
Wait a minute.
I haven't pressed dial yet,

357
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:10,033
- but someone's talking already.
- [LAUGHTER SFX]

358
00:15:10,033 --> 00:15:13,500
You know,<i> GGV</i> has been high tech
when we moved to GMA.

359
00:15:13,500 --> 00:15:17,967
With how strong the signal
is from their radio tower,

360
00:15:17,967 --> 00:15:20,133
even when you're just
holding your phone,

361
00:15:20,133 --> 00:15:21,633
the person you're about
to contact

362
00:15:21,633 --> 00:15:23,133
already knows
you're going to call them.

363
00:15:23,133 --> 00:15:24,967
- Oh, right.
- Right?

364
00:15:24,967 --> 00:15:27,733
But I texted someone
to hurry up and come here

365
00:15:27,733 --> 00:15:29,233
because I wanted to talk to her.

366
00:15:29,233 --> 00:15:31,233
- Do you know who I texted?
- [VERNA] Who was it?

367
00:15:31,233 --> 00:15:32,433
It's Annette herself.

368
00:15:32,433 --> 00:15:35,633
- [LAUGHING]
- Kidding! I'm just kidding.

369
00:15:35,667 --> 00:15:37,467
[VICE] It's not Miss Annette.

370
00:15:37,467 --> 00:15:38,633
It's this one.

371
00:15:38,833 --> 00:15:41,000
- Where is he?
- I heard him say "Hello."

372
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:43,767
Maybe, there were
some crossed lines.

373
00:15:43,767 --> 00:15:45,767
- Huh? Crossed lines?
- Crossed lines?

374
00:15:45,767 --> 00:15:49,000
Ah, here we go.
Let's give him a call.

375
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:52,000
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

376
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:53,467
- Who could it be?
- What happened?

377
00:15:53,467 --> 00:15:55,467
You know, is that
really your phone?

378
00:15:55,467 --> 00:15:58,467
You can afford a new home,
but not a new phone?

379
00:15:58,467 --> 00:15:59,467
My gosh!

380
00:15:59,467 --> 00:16:01,433
Ah, there it is.

381
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:05,467
Would you like me to
put the call on speaker?

382
00:16:05,467 --> 00:16:07,000
[AUDIENCE] Yes!

383
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:10,000
Or should I connect it
through Bluetooth?

384
00:16:10,033 --> 00:16:11,200
[LAUGHTER SFX]

385
00:16:11,200 --> 00:16:12,200
And when I connect it,
you'll hear,

386
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:14,367
"The Bluetooth device
is connected."

387
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:17,433
There, here we go!

388
00:16:17,433 --> 00:16:18,967
[LINE RINGING]

389
00:16:18,967 --> 00:16:20,100
[TETAY] Oh, it's ringing.

390
00:16:21,233 --> 00:16:22,433
[ALDEN] Hello?

391
00:16:22,433 --> 00:16:24,233
[AUDIENCE CHEERING, SQUEALING]

392
00:16:24,233 --> 00:16:25,733
[ALDEN] Hello, Vice!

393
00:16:25,733 --> 00:16:26,967
Hello?

394
00:16:26,967 --> 00:16:28,400
[ALDEN] Yes, hello?

395
00:16:28,967 --> 00:16:31,433
Um, sorry, it's a bit noisy
in my house

396
00:16:31,433 --> 00:16:34,233
because I'm having
a house blessing.

397
00:16:34,233 --> 00:16:37,733
So I have a lot of visitors
who came here,

398
00:16:37,733 --> 00:16:39,733
but there's not a lot of
attractive people among them.

399
00:16:39,733 --> 00:16:40,733
[LAUGHTER SFX]

400
00:16:40,733 --> 00:16:42,967
So I am looking for
a handsome visitor.

401
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,367
Um, hello?

402
00:16:44,367 --> 00:16:46,367
- [ALDEN]<i> Hello? Ah...
</i>- Where are you?

403
00:16:46,367 --> 00:16:48,167
[ALDEN] I think
I'm available today.

404
00:16:48,167 --> 00:16:50,167
[AUDIENCE SQUEALING]

405
00:16:50,167 --> 00:16:51,867
Oh my god!

406
00:16:51,867 --> 00:16:56,100
It's just that I have a new home
and I wanted to show it to you.

407
00:16:56,100 --> 00:16:59,267
[ALDEN]<i> Is that so?
</i> I like that. I really do.

408
00:16:59,267 --> 00:17:02,100
But where are you right now?

409
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:04,467
[ALDEN]<i> I'm just
</i> around the area.

410
00:17:04,467 --> 00:17:06,100
- Ah.
<i> - Should I come there?</i>

411
00:17:06,100 --> 00:17:08,100
- What did you say?
<i> - Should I come there?</i>

412
00:17:08,100 --> 00:17:09,267
- It's up to you.
- [AUDIENCE SQUEALING]

413
00:17:09,267 --> 00:17:10,767
[LAUGHING, CHEERING]

414
00:17:10,767 --> 00:17:12,267
- [TETAY] You sound so demure!
- [VERNA] How was it again?

415
00:17:12,267 --> 00:17:14,100
[ALDEN] But it seems like
there's a lot of people there.

416
00:17:14,100 --> 00:17:15,867
<i> I don't want to be a bother.</i>

417
00:17:15,900 --> 00:17:17,033
What did you say?

418
00:17:17,033 --> 00:17:18,067
[ALDEN]<i> It seems like
</i> there's a lot of people

419
00:17:18,067 --> 00:17:19,233
<i> I don't want to be a bother.</i>

420
00:17:19,233 --> 00:17:20,433
- [AUDIENCE CHEERING, SQUEALING]
- Oh no!

421
00:17:20,433 --> 00:17:22,633
Don't mind them.
Those were just the dogs.

422
00:17:22,633 --> 00:17:25,633
They'll be asleep already
by 10:30PM.

423
00:17:25,633 --> 00:17:27,433
[VICE] Um, you can come--

424
00:17:27,433 --> 00:17:29,633
So, will you be here soon?

425
00:17:29,633 --> 00:17:33,833
[ALDEN]<i> Yes, I think
</i> I'll be there in five minutes.

426
00:17:33,833 --> 00:17:34,900
- Ah!
- [VERNA] Whoa!

427
00:17:34,900 --> 00:17:37,033
Oh, you're quick.
You'll just take five minutes.

428
00:17:37,033 --> 00:17:38,533
I last for quite a long time.

429
00:17:38,533 --> 00:17:39,967
- [VERNA CHUCKLES]
- [ALDEN] I'll be there soon.

430
00:17:39,967 --> 00:17:43,733
- [DOORBELL RINGING]
- [VICE GASPS]

431
00:17:43,733 --> 00:17:45,733
Wait a second,
someone's ringing the doorbell.

432
00:17:45,733 --> 00:17:47,967
- [DOORBELL RINGING]
- Hello?

433
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:51,167
I think our call ended
all of a sudden.

434
00:17:51,167 --> 00:17:52,667
[AUDIENCE SQUEALING]

435
00:17:52,667 --> 00:17:53,933
[VICE] Wait a minute.

436
00:17:54,267 --> 00:17:56,467
By the way you look, shouldn't
you be the one opening the door?

437
00:17:56,467 --> 00:17:59,000
- [LAUGHTER SFX]
- Fine, I'll open the door.

438
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:01,767
Our furniture is new,
so don't sit on it like that!

439
00:18:01,767 --> 00:18:04,567
Maybe it's the water delivery.
Hurry up.

440
00:18:04,567 --> 00:18:07,067
- Who is it? How impatient!
- Who could it be?

441
00:18:07,067 --> 00:18:08,300
Who? What?

442
00:18:08,300 --> 00:18:10,267
- How do we even open the door?
- [TETAY] Just push it.

443
00:18:10,267 --> 00:18:11,467
- [TETAY GASPS]
- [VERNA EXCLAIMS]

444
00:18:11,467 --> 00:18:15,000
Oh my god! He's finally here!

445
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:17,400
<i>Gandang Gabi Vice!
Hello, everyone!</i>

446
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:19,933
My friend here is
so easy to talk to!

447
00:18:19,933 --> 00:18:21,700
- [VERNA] He's already here!
- [TETAY EXCLAIMS]

448
00:18:21,700 --> 00:18:23,900
My god, Alden!

449
00:18:24,633 --> 00:18:26,433
Gosh, how rowdy!

450
00:18:26,433 --> 00:18:27,633
[LAUGHTER SFX]

451
00:18:27,633 --> 00:18:29,433
[AUDIENCE CHANTING]
Alden! Alden!

452
00:18:29,433 --> 00:18:31,433
What a surprise, right?

453
00:18:31,433 --> 00:18:32,833
- Hello, everyone!
- [TETAY] Fantastic!

454
00:18:32,833 --> 00:18:34,633
- Good evening to you all!
- How explosive!

455
00:18:34,633 --> 00:18:38,100
<i> - Gandang Gabi,</i> Alden!
<i> - Gandang Gabi,</i> everyone!

456
00:18:38,733 --> 00:18:39,967
[ALDEN] Here, I brought a gift.

457
00:18:39,967 --> 00:18:42,433
That's how quickly
I get prepared.

458
00:18:42,433 --> 00:18:45,433
From our phone call, I was able
to buy a housewarming gift,

459
00:18:45,433 --> 00:18:46,633
and I was able to get here
right away.

460
00:18:46,633 --> 00:18:47,967
You're truly a good friend!

461
00:18:47,967 --> 00:18:49,433
He really is a reliable friend.

462
00:18:49,433 --> 00:18:51,233
Anytime you call him,
he is available.

463
00:18:51,233 --> 00:18:53,433
- He's always there.
- He won't say no to you.

464
00:18:53,433 --> 00:18:55,233
[VICE] They're my housemates.

465
00:18:55,267 --> 00:18:56,767
That's Tetay and that's...

466
00:18:56,767 --> 00:19:00,000
That's our newly-bought
pit bull.

467
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:01,467
[LAUGHTER SFX]

468
00:19:01,467 --> 00:19:03,067
[VICE] Verna, meet Alden.

469
00:19:03,067 --> 00:19:07,067
People may not know it,
but I'm a big fan of Verna.

470
00:19:07,067 --> 00:19:09,267
- Ooh!
- Yes!

471
00:19:09,267 --> 00:19:12,467
I'm not kidding,
I watch her on Showtime.

472
00:19:12,467 --> 00:19:14,467
On Muse...
What's your segment again?

473
00:19:14,467 --> 00:19:16,000
- Breaking Muse.
- Breaking Muse!

474
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:19,933
That time when you were
judging Jessy Mendiola.

475
00:19:19,933 --> 00:19:21,500
I don't know what to feel
about it, but you were great!

476
00:19:21,500 --> 00:19:25,000
And you also sang<i> Chandelier
</i>but you were the chandelier.

477
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:27,467
And I just found out
recently that...

478
00:19:27,800 --> 00:19:30,800
we had a mutual friend from
where she used to live at.

479
00:19:30,833 --> 00:19:32,233
- And she knew...
- [VICE] Who was it?

480
00:19:32,233 --> 00:19:33,433
- It's Michael Bristol.
- Yeah.

481
00:19:33,433 --> 00:19:38,133
She also knows my executive
assistant, Mama Ten.

482
00:19:38,133 --> 00:19:39,967
We really have a lot of
mutual friends because

