- [AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

720
00:31:13,533 --> 00:31:15,867
- In<i> It's Showtime.
</i>- I resign, I resign.

721
00:31:16,400 --> 00:31:18,600
I resign. Lord, sorry, Lord!

722
00:31:19,067 --> 00:31:23,000
[VICE] Right. For them,
it was just a natural occurence.

723
00:31:24,733 --> 00:31:25,700
[ALDEN] Save me, guys...

724
00:31:25,700 --> 00:31:28,000
For us, it was like...

725
00:31:28,000 --> 00:31:32,333
a calamity that the NDRRMC
failed to warn us about.

726
00:31:32,333 --> 00:31:34,700
- [LAUGH TRACK]
- We weren't ready. Like,

727
00:31:34,700 --> 00:31:37,500
what? The typhoon is here
already?! We had no idea.

728
00:31:37,500 --> 00:31:41,067
And it was a super typhoon
to boot!

729
00:31:41,067 --> 00:31:44,100
That's why you took
the entire nation by storm.

730
00:31:44,133 --> 00:31:45,200
[VERNA] Woah!

731
00:31:45,200 --> 00:31:47,800
That's why it's called
AlDub Nation, right?

732
00:31:47,800 --> 00:31:49,667
The Philippines became
an AlDub Nation.

733
00:31:49,667 --> 00:31:52,300
But it was truly entertaining.

734
00:31:52,300 --> 00:31:54,867
- [ALDEN] Thank you, thank you.
- I peek at it sometimes.

735
00:31:54,867 --> 00:31:57,867
- [LAUGHTER]
- [LAUGH TRACK]

736
00:31:57,867 --> 00:32:02,133
Of course I had to watch it
to know what is going on.

737
00:32:02,133 --> 00:32:04,333
Right? What is going on?
Why are they such a hit?

738
00:32:04,333 --> 00:32:05,667
So I explained,

739
00:32:05,867 --> 00:32:09,300
"It's fun. This and that
is happening."

740
00:32:09,300 --> 00:32:10,700
And then I pray everyday,

741
00:32:10,700 --> 00:32:12,433
"Lord, please make this happen."

742
00:32:12,433 --> 00:32:14,400
[LAUGHTER]

743
00:32:14,400 --> 00:32:16,233
But it was really amazing.

744
00:32:16,767 --> 00:32:19,467
But were you guys aware
of what was happening to us?

745
00:32:19,467 --> 00:32:21,000
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

746
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:22,133
We are.

747
00:32:22,133 --> 00:32:23,467
So where's your conscience?

748
00:32:23,467 --> 00:32:24,900
- [ALDEN] It was...
- [AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

749
00:32:24,900 --> 00:32:26,300
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

750
00:32:26,300 --> 00:32:27,500
[TETAY] That's right.

751
00:32:27,500 --> 00:32:29,033
- [LAUGHTER]
-[ AUDIENCE APPLAUDING]

752
00:32:29,033 --> 00:32:30,700
- [VICE] Right?
- That's right!

753
00:32:30,700 --> 00:32:33,200
That's why I haven't forgotten
what Miss Annette said

754
00:32:33,200 --> 00:32:34,267
when we had a meeting.

755
00:32:34,267 --> 00:32:36,267
She said, "What's good
about collaborations?"

756
00:32:36,267 --> 00:32:39,867
She said, "It's a win-win
situation."

757
00:32:39,867 --> 00:32:43,300
It doesn't always have to be
a winner and then a loser.

758
00:32:43,300 --> 00:32:46,067
Miss Annette said,
"As a Christian,

759
00:32:46,067 --> 00:32:49,867
it doesn't make us happy
if we win while someone loses

760
00:32:49,900 --> 00:32:51,467
when we could all win."

761
00:32:52,067 --> 00:32:54,200
So why didn't you guys
apply that?

762
00:32:54,200 --> 00:32:56,067
[VICE] We were knocked out.

763
00:32:56,067 --> 00:32:57,467
[TETAY] Answer, Alden!

764
00:32:57,967 --> 00:33:00,333
Save me. Nelson Canlas!

765
00:33:00,333 --> 00:33:02,967
- Please, Nelson Canlas.
- That Nelson Canlas too.

766
00:33:02,967 --> 00:33:05,233
That's right. He reports
your news every night!

767
00:33:05,233 --> 00:33:06,700
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

768
00:33:06,700 --> 00:33:08,800
- It's all about AlDub!
- [LAUGHTER]

769
00:33:08,800 --> 00:33:10,467
No but, when I watched it
I thought,

770
00:33:10,467 --> 00:33:12,500
"This is really magical."

771
00:33:12,500 --> 00:33:16,500
It was so fun to watch.
Really entertaining.

772
00:33:16,500 --> 00:33:18,500
It was really an escape, right?

773
00:33:18,500 --> 00:33:20,833
When you watch it, you'll really
forget what you're doing,

774
00:33:20,833 --> 00:33:22,333
your problems,
what you're going through,

775
00:33:22,367 --> 00:33:24,633
because you'll tune in to it
no matter what.

776
00:33:24,633 --> 00:33:27,733
- And I was so mad at the...
- The granny?

777
00:33:27,733 --> 00:33:29,533
- Yes, at Granny Nidora.
- Yeah.

778
00:33:29,533 --> 00:33:31,600
At JoWaPao. I was infuriated!

779
00:33:31,600 --> 00:33:34,167
Because they were so good!

780
00:33:34,167 --> 00:33:38,100
I thought that they were
really funny.

781
00:33:38,100 --> 00:33:40,100
Then I talked to Vhong Navarro
and Jhong Hilario.

782
00:33:40,100 --> 00:33:43,133
- "Vhong...
- [AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

783
00:33:43,133 --> 00:33:44,633
can you put a bow on your head?"

784
00:33:44,633 --> 00:33:46,500
[LAUGHTER]

785
00:33:46,500 --> 00:33:48,433
Oh, and let me share
this too, Vice.

786
00:33:48,433 --> 00:33:51,100
During that time when we
were doing everything,

787
00:33:52,533 --> 00:33:55,667
until after Tamang Panahon,

788
00:33:56,333 --> 00:33:57,633
we didn't have a script.

789
00:33:58,033 --> 00:34:00,333
- [VICE] I know!
- We had no script at all.

790
00:34:00,333 --> 00:34:04,733
Basically, we'll just play along
with the scenario

791
00:34:04,733 --> 00:34:05,967
on where we left off

792
00:34:05,967 --> 00:34:08,100
- the episode before.
- Alright then, big shots!

793
00:34:08,100 --> 00:34:10,333
- [AUDIENCE LAUGHING]
- [ALDEN] I was just explaining.

794
00:34:11,400 --> 00:34:12,833
I was just explaining things.

795
00:34:12,833 --> 00:34:14,167
- [TETAY] Do that face again.
- Okay, sorry.

796
00:34:14,167 --> 00:34:15,733
- [ALDEN] I was just joking.
- [TETAY LAUGHING]

797
00:34:15,733 --> 00:34:17,733
Because while he was recalling
happy memories,

798
00:34:17,733 --> 00:34:20,533
- [TETAY] Yes.
- I was recalling the sad ones.

799
00:34:20,533 --> 00:34:22,867
- [VERNA] The sadness!
- Right? For him they were happy

800
00:34:22,867 --> 00:34:24,767
- while for me, it's traumatic.
- [AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

801
00:34:24,767 --> 00:34:27,067
Plus we're reminiscing
at the same time. Okay.

802
00:34:27,067 --> 00:34:28,433
As you were saying.

803
00:34:28,433 --> 00:34:30,400
There was no script and um...

804
00:34:30,967 --> 00:34:34,000
we were just waiting
for instructions

805
00:34:34,000 --> 00:34:37,367
through our in-ear monitors
and it was live.

806
00:34:37,367 --> 00:34:38,667
- [VICE] So you had in-ears.
- We did.

807
00:34:38,667 --> 00:34:40,267
- You'll hear instructions?
- Yes, yes.

808
00:34:40,267 --> 00:34:42,300
Oh, okay because
at<i> It's Showtime</i> we don't.

809
00:34:42,300 --> 00:34:44,733
- [ALDEN] Period!
- [TETAY] Woah!

810
00:34:45,100 --> 00:34:46,133
[VERNA] Yes!

811
00:34:46,133 --> 00:34:48,933
That's why see? Our ratings
were so low.

812
00:34:48,933 --> 00:34:50,700
Our ratings were so low!

813
00:34:50,700 --> 00:34:52,733
My god! We should've used
in-ears!

814
00:34:52,733 --> 00:34:55,300
- [LAUGHTER]
- So that's why!

815
00:34:55,300 --> 00:34:57,300
- [TETAY] It's cheap too!
- We should've used in-ears.

816
00:34:57,300 --> 00:35:00,433
If I'm not mistaken,
there was an episode

817
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:02,567
where your ratings
were above 40%

818
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:05,367
and our ratings were 5% or 4%.

819
00:35:05,867 --> 00:35:07,967
Yeah. Can I see
your reaction again?

820
00:35:08,367 --> 00:35:09,433
I had no idea.

821
00:35:09,433 --> 00:35:10,733
The gap was that huge.

822
00:35:10,733 --> 00:35:12,200
And that time,

823
00:35:12,400 --> 00:35:13,833
while you were waiting

824
00:35:13,833 --> 00:35:15,700
for directions
through your in-ear,

825
00:35:15,700 --> 00:35:18,267
I was waiting for the management
to call me

826
00:35:18,267 --> 00:35:20,200
and tell me that the show
will be canceled.

827
00:35:20,200 --> 00:35:21,300
I swear.

828
00:35:21,300 --> 00:35:22,633
I was ready for it.

829
00:35:22,633 --> 00:35:24,333
- [TETAY] For real.
- [VERNA] Aww...

830
00:35:24,333 --> 00:35:25,533
I swear.

831
00:35:26,467 --> 00:35:32,433
It was one of the darkest,
heaviest, saddest,

832
00:35:32,433 --> 00:35:35,967
no kidding, saddest stages
of It's Showtime

833
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:38,967
as well as me as an entertainer.

834
00:35:39,167 --> 00:35:41,567
It was really hard to bear

835
00:35:41,567 --> 00:35:44,867
but it was also one of the
things I'm thankful for.

836
00:35:44,867 --> 00:35:46,833
I learned a lot of things.

837
00:35:46,833 --> 00:35:48,800
That experience we had,

838
00:35:49,300 --> 00:35:51,533
made our program stronger.

839
00:35:51,533 --> 00:35:52,667
Like what we said,

840
00:35:53,200 --> 00:35:58,600
we have nothing
to be scared of now.

841
00:35:58,600 --> 00:36:00,100
AlDub already happened,

842
00:36:00,100 --> 00:36:01,933
is there anything
bigger than them?

843
00:36:01,933 --> 00:36:03,267
If we were able
to get through it,

844
00:36:03,267 --> 00:36:05,633
then we can go through anything.

845
00:36:06,000 --> 00:36:08,433
AlDub was so huge.

846
00:36:08,433 --> 00:36:11,033
Alden, Maine.

847
00:36:11,067 --> 00:36:14,700
You know, there was one time
when I went home in Tambunting.

848
00:36:14,700 --> 00:36:16,533
Because back then, I visit home
every now and then

849
00:36:16,533 --> 00:36:18,733
and give away a little something
and stuff.

850
00:36:18,733 --> 00:36:19,700
Hanging out with them.

851
00:36:19,700 --> 00:36:21,733
One time, after I got out
of my car,

852
00:36:22,100 --> 00:36:26,100
the kids were chanting,
"AlDub! AlDub!"

853
00:36:26,100 --> 00:36:27,400
- I swear.
- [AUDIENCE EXCLAIMING]

854
00:36:27,400 --> 00:36:29,033
I went to the bathroom
and cried a little.

855
00:36:29,033 --> 00:36:30,100
I was like...

856
00:36:30,633 --> 00:36:32,333
mind you, this is my turf

857
00:36:32,333 --> 00:36:35,500
but they're still chanting
for AlDub.

858
00:36:35,800 --> 00:36:40,733
So I said, you can't really
explain this.

859
00:36:40,933 --> 00:36:43,300
This country loves them so much.

860
00:36:43,333 --> 00:36:46,033
- [AUDIENCE APPLAUDING]
-[VICE] So I told It's Showtime

861
00:36:46,267 --> 00:36:50,133
that I was actually mad at them.
Because of them,

862
00:36:50,133 --> 00:36:52,667
I couldn't watch AlDub
regularly.

863
00:36:52,667 --> 00:36:54,700
- [AUDIENCE LAUGHING]
- I'm always behind.

864
00:36:54,700 --> 00:36:56,000
I just ask people for updates.

865
00:36:56,000 --> 00:36:57,600
<i> It's Showtime</i> was such
a hindrance!

866
00:36:57,600 --> 00:36:59,667
- Adjust its time slot!
- [ALDEN LAUGHING]

867
00:36:59,667 --> 00:37:02,133
I couldn't watch Alden
and Maine.

868
00:37:02,333 --> 00:37:04,533
It was crazy. But,

869
00:37:04,767 --> 00:37:07,400
I told this to<i> It's Showtime.
</i>The Philippines is so lucky

870
00:37:07,400 --> 00:37:10,400
to have experienced AlDub
in this lifetime.

871
00:37:10,400 --> 00:37:11,600
- [ALDEN] Thank you, Vice.
- Right? It's different.

872
00:37:11,600 --> 00:37:13,433
It was a phenomenon.

873
00:37:13,433 --> 00:37:15,267
It was just so fun, right?

874
00:37:15,267 --> 00:37:18,167
You guys made so many people
happy.

875
00:37:18,200 --> 00:37:21,167
After all, that's our role
as entertainers, right?

876
00:37:21,167 --> 00:37:26,400
To give our fellow countrymen
a moment to escape

877
00:37:26,400 --> 00:37:28,767
from, of course,
their daily lives

878
00:37:28,767 --> 00:37:33,633
especially those
who are underprivileged.

879
00:37:33,633 --> 00:37:37,900
It's like their only way
to forget...

880
00:37:38,100 --> 00:37:40,467
- what's happening.
- Yeah, and it gave hope.

881
00:37:40,467 --> 00:37:41,800
You gave them hope.

882
00:37:42,100 --> 00:37:45,200
Right? Just like in the story,

883
00:37:45,200 --> 00:37:47,400
those stories are effective.
The fairy tale-like ones.

884
00:37:47,400 --> 00:37:51,133
Like, a man who is so handsome
like a prince charming

885
00:37:51,167 --> 00:37:56,600
with a girl who's simple
and humble,

886
00:37:56,600 --> 00:37:59,233
a<i> Cinderella</i> story, right?

887
00:37:59,233 --> 00:38:01,400
Where they'll think,
"Oh, so there's hope.

888
00:38:01,400 --> 00:38:03,967
I don't need to be fair-skinned

889
00:38:03,967 --> 00:38:07,300
for someone to fall for me
and look at me.

890
00:38:07,300 --> 00:38:09,333
I don't need to be immediately
popular

891
00:38:09,333 --> 00:38:12,033
for a popular person
to pay attention to me."

892
00:38:12,033 --> 00:38:17,700
You guys gave people hope
that such a thing is possible.

893
00:38:17,933 --> 00:38:21,967
And it's important that as you
watch a noontime show,

894
00:38:21,967 --> 00:38:24,600
you feel hopeful.

895
00:38:25,067 --> 00:38:26,600
- Right?
- That's right, Vice.

896
00:38:26,833 --> 00:38:27,933
[VICE] But, again...

897
00:38:28,233 --> 00:38:30,000
- [LAUGHTER]
- Get him!

898
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:30,967
[VICE SIGHS HEAVILY]

899
00:38:30,967 --> 00:38:32,300
Why are you guys
just laughing over there?

900
00:38:32,300 --> 00:38:33,833
Because you've really hurt him!

901
00:38:33,833 --> 00:38:37,533
[VICE] Exactly. You've mentioned
about the memo, right?

902
00:38:37,533 --> 00:38:38,533
Right?

903
00:38:38,533 --> 00:38:40,000
I also have a memo for the gays.

904
00:38:40,000 --> 00:38:40,967
[TETAY] What is, sis? [WHEEZES]

905
00:38:40,967 --> 00:38:42,967
Don't post about AlDub
on social media.

906
00:38:42,967 --> 00:38:45,567
Because even on social media,
on FaceBook, Twitter,

907
00:38:45,567 --> 00:38:46,767
they're all over it!

908
00:38:46,967 --> 00:38:48,633
- Right?
- Hey, Nelson Canlas!

909
00:38:48,633 --> 00:38:50,000
You're the one who report
about it!

910
00:38:50,000 --> 00:38:52,267
Do you guys know
that he's depressed?

911
00:38:52,267 --> 00:38:53,500
He won't even get up to eat!

912
00:38:53,500 --> 00:38:55,900
- Right, Tetay?
- Yes! We went to his place,

913
00:38:55,900 --> 00:38:57,133
you have no idea!

914
00:38:57,167 --> 00:38:59,833
"Vice, let's eat.", "Later.
Just stay with me for now."

915
00:38:59,833 --> 00:39:01,500
It was that bad, Alden!

916
00:39:01,500 --> 00:39:02,867
- [ALDEN] Hold your horses.
- And you don't know about it.

917
00:39:02,867 --> 00:39:04,567
Wait, what about us?

918
00:39:04,567 --> 00:39:07,667
It's our sister! He couldn't
even eat! You're so insensitive!

919
00:39:07,667 --> 00:39:10,033
My baby wouldn't even eat!

920
00:39:10,033 --> 00:39:11,767
- I said sorry!
- Now you come here

921
00:39:11,767 --> 00:39:13,800
just to revisit those memories?

922
00:39:13,800 --> 00:39:15,267
- [TETAY] That's right!
- [AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

923
00:39:15,267 --> 00:39:17,233
- [ALDEN] Uh-oh...
- You're so cruel, Alden.

924
00:39:17,233 --> 00:39:19,833
- [ALDEN] Ow.
- [AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

925
00:39:19,833 --> 00:39:22,367
- Apologize to our sister!
- No.

926
00:39:22,367 --> 00:39:23,933
- We're good now.
- [TETAY] Oh, okay. Sorry.

927
00:39:23,933 --> 00:39:26,067
I never took it personally.

928
00:39:26,067 --> 00:39:28,933
Even before. Every time
we saw each other

929
00:39:28,933 --> 00:39:33,000
during events, I'm not lying,
Alden is really kind.

930
00:39:33,033 --> 00:39:35,367
- Really kind!
- No matter where we meet,

931
00:39:35,367 --> 00:39:38,000
I'm even the one
who's a little awkward.

932
00:39:38,000 --> 00:39:39,733
- [TETAY] It's like that, huh?
- Because of course,

933
00:39:39,733 --> 00:39:44,733
since it's a competition,
people often think

934
00:39:44,733 --> 00:39:45,967
that there's tension.

935
00:39:45,967 --> 00:39:48,833
Like, "Oh, it's Vice and Alden!"
when they see us together.

936
00:39:48,833 --> 00:39:52,067
Alden would be the one to run
while shouting, "Miss Vice!"

937
00:39:52,067 --> 00:39:54,467
He's very kind, smells good,
and so handsome.

938
00:39:54,467 --> 00:39:55,800
- [VERNA] Wow!
- [TETAY] Very polite.

939
00:39:55,800 --> 00:39:57,667
- [VERNA] True!
- [VICE] So every time we meet

940
00:39:57,667 --> 00:39:59,300
and I see Alden, we'll be
greeting each other.

941
00:39:59,300 --> 00:40:01,800
"Alden, hi! Hi!"

942
00:40:02,167 --> 00:40:04,667
- [LAUGHTER]
- [SILLY SFX]

943
00:40:04,700 --> 00:40:06,333
Alden and I are all good.

944
00:40:06,333 --> 00:40:08,167
That's why he shouldn't
apologize to me.

945
00:40:08,167 --> 00:40:10,167
But I will give you one chance.

946
00:40:10,767 --> 00:40:13,233
Apologize
to the Madlang people.

947
00:40:13,233 --> 00:40:15,433
[LAUGHTER]

948
00:40:15,433 --> 00:40:18,233
- Um...
- [VICE] You've really hurt us.

949
00:40:18,233 --> 00:40:20,633
Um... [CLEARS THROAT]
Where's the camera? Is it this?

950
00:40:21,100 --> 00:40:22,433
Ah, so...

951
00:40:22,433 --> 00:40:26,100
To the Madlang People,
to the people behind Showtime--

952
00:40:27,000 --> 00:40:29,200
- Let's pretend this is in 2016.
- Sure.

953
00:40:29,200 --> 00:40:31,067
You really want to take me
back to that year, huh?

954
00:40:31,067 --> 00:40:32,833
[LAUGHTER]

955
00:40:32,833 --> 00:40:35,300
That was 10 years ago,
but it still hurts.

956
00:40:35,300 --> 00:40:37,267
[SILLY SFX, LAUGH TRACK PLAYING]

957
00:40:37,300 --> 00:40:41,300
To the hosts of It's Showtime,

958
00:40:41,300 --> 00:40:45,000
most especially
to Miss Vice Ganda,

959
00:40:45,000 --> 00:40:48,067
I'd like to apologize for
whatever wrong we've done.

960
00:40:48,067 --> 00:40:52,233
If we did something out
of pure intentions, but--

961
00:40:52,700 --> 00:40:56,467
As you said earlier, Vice,

962
00:40:56,467 --> 00:40:58,100
we have only one intention,

963
00:40:58,100 --> 00:41:00,100
and that is
to make people happy.

964
00:41:00,100 --> 00:41:02,567
[AUDIENCE CHEERING, APPLAUDING]

965
00:41:02,567 --> 00:41:04,400
But still,
I'd like to apologize because

966
00:41:04,400 --> 00:41:06,067
I know how heavy it is.

967
00:41:06,067 --> 00:41:07,333
I honestly don't know

968
00:41:07,333 --> 00:41:09,033
if you're joking around
or being serious.

969
00:41:09,033 --> 00:41:11,500
C'mon, I'm being serious here.

970
00:41:11,533 --> 00:41:14,133
- [ALDEN] Ah, really?
- [LAUGHS]

971
00:41:14,133 --> 00:41:15,900
No, I'm just messing around.

972
00:41:15,900 --> 00:41:18,100
- [TETAY] No, this is for Vice.
- What is this for?

973
00:41:18,100 --> 00:41:19,800
They said
you were about to cry.

974
00:41:19,800 --> 00:41:22,267
Didn't I tell you
I'd call if I needed you?!

975
00:41:22,267 --> 00:41:23,967
[VERNA] You're about
to cry, Meme.

976
00:41:23,967 --> 00:41:25,667
See, we're just
concerned for you.

977
00:41:25,667 --> 00:41:26,867
We love you, Vice.

978
00:41:26,867 --> 00:41:28,267
Yeah, but...

979
00:41:28,267 --> 00:41:31,600
- I am very grateful to Alden--
- [ALDEN] Can I just say,

980
00:41:31,600 --> 00:41:38,233
I won't forget the first
surreal moment where

981
00:41:38,233 --> 00:41:41,833
it was my first time being
a guest on It's Showtime.

982
00:41:42,367 --> 00:41:46,133
Before you introduced us,
you said something--

983
00:41:46,167 --> 00:41:48,133
I think it was a promotion
for Family of Two,

984
00:41:48,133 --> 00:41:49,500
I was with Sharon Cuneta.

985
00:41:50,067 --> 00:41:51,300
Ah.

986
00:41:51,300 --> 00:41:53,300
It seemed strange, this is--

987
00:41:53,300 --> 00:41:56,567
This is something
we never expected.

988
00:41:56,567 --> 00:41:58,333
When I heard the words
you were saying,

989
00:41:58,333 --> 00:42:00,067
that's when I realized,

990
00:42:00,533 --> 00:42:03,000
"Wow, who would've thought

991
00:42:03,000 --> 00:42:06,233
that after all these years
and after all that happened,

992
00:42:07,033 --> 00:42:12,600
we'd end up being here together
with one goal in the industry."

993
00:42:12,600 --> 00:42:17,067
And all those times,
we were okay!

994
00:42:17,100 --> 00:42:18,533
We were all fine.

995
00:42:18,533 --> 00:42:22,100
Our shows just aired at the same
time, and during those times

996
00:42:22,100 --> 00:42:23,933
our fans and supporters
were at each other's throats.

997
00:42:23,933 --> 00:42:25,200
But

998
00:42:25,200 --> 00:42:27,167
<i> Eat Bulaga!</i> and<i> It's Showtime
<i>have always been okay.</i></i>

999
00:42:27,167 --> 00:42:29,767
We don't have any bad blood.
They were kind to us.

1000
00:42:29,767 --> 00:42:32,067
That's why we don't have
anything bad to say about them.

1001
00:42:32,067 --> 00:42:33,933
- Right? That's why
- Yes, Vice.

1002
00:42:33,933 --> 00:42:39,533
Whenever I see you, my aura
feels natural and sincere.

1003
00:42:39,533 --> 00:42:42,067
My face lights up
whenever I see Alden.

1004
00:42:42,067 --> 00:42:44,367
Also, Alden just
looks very handsome.

1005
00:42:44,367 --> 00:42:46,000
- [TETAY] It's true.
- [VERNA] It's true.

1006
00:42:46,000 --> 00:42:47,767
[VICE] Especially now--

1007
00:42:47,767 --> 00:42:49,033
Now you're both acting
fine around me!

1008
00:42:49,033 --> 00:42:51,600
No, what Vice said was true,
you are handsome!

1009
00:42:51,633 --> 00:42:53,467
[ALDEN] You were both
so heartless with me earlier!

1010
00:42:53,467 --> 00:42:55,367
[TETAY] You were in
the wrong earlier.

1011
00:42:55,367 --> 00:42:57,733
[ALDEN] Son of a--
Okay, okay, sorry!

1012
00:42:57,733 --> 00:42:59,200
- He got mad!
-[VICE] We're fine now.

1013
00:42:59,200 --> 00:43:00,067
[ALDEN] Sorry, sorry, Vice.

1014
00:43:00,067 --> 00:43:02,567
I told him earlier
that he looked

1015
00:43:02,567 --> 00:43:04,367
younger because he lost weight!

1016
00:43:04,367 --> 00:43:07,667
You look handsome.
Are-- are you eating well?

1017
00:43:07,667 --> 00:43:08,833
- I am.
- [VICE] Are you tired?

1018
00:43:08,833 --> 00:43:10,033
You look like you've
lost some weight.

1019
00:43:10,033 --> 00:43:14,167
As i said in an interview
with Nelson Canlas--

1020
00:43:14,867 --> 00:43:17,700
since he's there,
I'm calling him out.

1021
00:43:17,700 --> 00:43:21,733
Now that I'm reaching
my mid-30s, going late 30s,

1022
00:43:21,733 --> 00:43:24,633
I'm also having a
slightly different perspective

1023
00:43:24,667 --> 00:43:26,800
on how I take on life.

1024
00:43:26,800 --> 00:43:32,167
The others are saying that
I'm still young, but for me,

1025
00:43:32,167 --> 00:43:33,300
the earlier, the better.

1026
00:43:33,300 --> 00:43:36,767
Right now, I'm a little
more intentional

1027
00:43:36,767 --> 00:43:38,767
with the things
I let in my life.

1028
00:43:38,767 --> 00:43:41,267
The number one thing,
of course, is what I eat.

1029
00:43:41,267 --> 00:43:43,567
- What do you eat now?
- My lifestyle.

1030
00:43:43,567 --> 00:43:45,267
Everything but in moderation.

1031
00:43:45,267 --> 00:43:48,733
- So, everything?
- Yes, I still eat those.

1032
00:43:48,733 --> 00:43:51,267
Don't the others shift
to being vegan?

1033
00:43:51,267 --> 00:43:52,267
[ALDEN] Yeah.

1034
00:43:52,267 --> 00:43:54,667
I take everything in moderation,

1035
00:43:54,667 --> 00:43:56,967
I also have a healthy
lifestyle, and I exercise.

1036
00:43:57,000 --> 00:43:59,533
Most especially a positive
outlook on life.

1037
00:43:59,533 --> 00:44:00,833
- Yes. That's important.
- Yes.

1038
00:44:00,833 --> 00:44:03,633
We're reducing
toxic people in our lives.

1039
00:44:03,633 --> 00:44:06,067
- That's true.
- [VERNA] True.

1040
00:44:06,067 --> 00:44:07,467
[VICE] That's true, right?

1041
00:44:07,467 --> 00:44:12,500
No matter what checkup
you do, multivitamins you take,

1042
00:44:12,500 --> 00:44:13,900
or suppliments you take,

1043
00:44:13,900 --> 00:44:16,800
if you're being surrounded
with too much negativity,

1044
00:44:16,800 --> 00:44:18,967
you'll be consumed by it,
and you'll get sick.

1045
00:44:18,967 --> 00:44:20,933
I'm all for that, 100%.

1046
00:44:20,933 --> 00:44:25,167
I actually feel shy.
You brought me wine, right?

1047
00:44:25,167 --> 00:44:26,633
- Yes, wine.
- You even brought me wine,

1048
00:44:26,633 --> 00:44:29,233
butwe don't have anything
to give you in return.

1049
00:44:29,233 --> 00:44:30,767
We have something here, Meme.

1050
00:44:30,800 --> 00:44:32,700
- [VICE] What food?
- Wait, let me heat her up.

1051
00:44:32,700 --> 00:44:34,200
- [LAUGHS] No, not me!
- [SILLY SFX PLAYING]

1052
00:44:34,200 --> 00:44:36,933
- We did some research, Meme.
- [VICE] Well, what is it?

1053
00:44:36,933 --> 00:44:39,467
We found out what
Alden's favorite food is.

1054
00:44:39,467 --> 00:44:41,067
- So, what is it?
- [VERNA] Yes.

1055
00:44:41,067 --> 00:44:42,733
Because I believe...

1056
00:44:43,900 --> 00:44:47,333
that a way to a man's heart
is through his stomach.

1057
00:44:47,333 --> 00:44:49,333
- Wow.
- Did you say stomach?

1058
00:44:49,333 --> 00:44:50,867
- Stomach!
- [ALDEN] Ah, stomach!

1059
00:44:50,867 --> 00:44:53,067
- [VICE IMITATES VERNA]
- Enough, girl!

1060
00:44:53,067 --> 00:44:54,900
You're so--
Wait, what is that?

1061
00:44:54,900 --> 00:44:56,433
[TETAY] We prepared spaghetti.

1062
00:44:56,433 --> 00:44:58,133
- Alden is very picky.
- [VICE] Is that what I saw

1063
00:44:58,133 --> 00:44:59,667
earlier?
The one in the plastic?

1064
00:44:59,667 --> 00:45:01,733
- [LAUGHTER]
- Did you cut open the end?

1065
00:45:01,733 --> 00:45:04,067
I actually saw Verna
eating it earlier.

1066
00:45:04,100 --> 00:45:06,433
We bought it from
a breakfast buffet, actually.

1067
00:45:06,433 --> 00:45:08,900
Don't say that in front of
our guest. It's embarrassing.

1068
00:45:08,900 --> 00:45:11,400
- Is that all?
- [TETAY] No, of course not.

1069
00:45:11,400 --> 00:45:12,800
- Come here and eat, Alden.
- Alden loves--

1070
00:45:12,800 --> 00:45:15,633
[VICE] You should go
there and eat, Alden.

1071
00:45:16,533 --> 00:45:17,467
[ALDEN] What?

1072
00:45:18,900 --> 00:45:21,133
That looks good. Wow.

1073
00:45:21,133 --> 00:45:22,567
Wait.

1074
00:45:22,567 --> 00:45:25,067
Where did this food come from?

1075
00:45:25,067 --> 00:45:27,567
Where-- Ah, Verna!

1076
00:45:27,567 --> 00:45:29,100
Someone will eat. Stay away.

1077
00:45:29,100 --> 00:45:30,800
- Wait, where is the...
- [SILLY SFX PLAYING]

1078
00:45:30,800 --> 00:45:32,100
- I'll go with you, Meme.
- What do you need?

1079
00:45:32,100 --> 00:45:34,333
Where's the lime and ketchup?

1080
00:45:34,333 --> 00:45:35,667
Oh, you need lime?

1081
00:45:35,667 --> 00:45:37,400
- Here's the lime.
- It's right there.

1082
00:45:38,633 --> 00:45:40,267
- Lime?
- Yes.

1083
00:45:40,267 --> 00:45:41,467
- Yes, and...
- Wow.

1084
00:45:42,267 --> 00:45:43,267
Lime...

1085
00:45:44,433 --> 00:45:45,833
- Here you go.
- This is embarrassing.

1086
00:45:45,833 --> 00:45:48,933
You were so against me earlier,
now you're serving me.

1087
00:45:48,933 --> 00:45:50,933
C'mon...

1088
00:45:50,933 --> 00:45:52,767
What's the lime for?
For the noodles?

1089
00:45:52,767 --> 00:45:54,767
- For the noodles.
- No, for the spaghetti.

1090
00:45:54,767 --> 00:45:55,633
- Hey!
- What?!

1091
00:45:56,100 --> 00:45:57,367
What?!

1092
00:45:57,367 --> 00:45:59,867
You add lime to your spaghetti?

1093
00:45:59,867 --> 00:46:01,400
- Why?!
- Yes.

1094
00:46:01,400 --> 00:46:04,567
This is my weird
food combination.

1095
00:46:04,567 --> 00:46:06,867
Actually,
it's not just spaghetti.

1096
00:46:06,867 --> 00:46:08,633
I love--

1097
00:46:09,600 --> 00:46:11,167
- Will you taste it?
- Yes.

1098
00:46:11,200 --> 00:46:14,067
- Let me add it first.
- You taste it first.

1099
00:46:14,500 --> 00:46:17,467
We don't have forks
so we should share--

1100
00:46:17,467 --> 00:46:19,400
[ALDEN] Yeah, sure! Go ahead!

1101
00:46:19,400 --> 00:46:20,767
No, uh...

1102
00:46:20,767 --> 00:46:22,967
Actually, Verna uses
her hands to eat spaghetti.

1103
00:46:22,967 --> 00:46:24,567
- [SILLY SFX PLAYING]
- It's true.

1104
00:46:24,567 --> 00:46:27,100
She also uses a toothpick
when she eats noodles.

1105
00:46:27,100 --> 00:46:29,467
That's our finger food.
Noodles.

1106
00:46:29,467 --> 00:46:30,567
Okay, so...

1107
00:46:30,567 --> 00:46:36,167
I love bending the usual
flavor of the food I eat.

1108
00:46:36,167 --> 00:46:38,300
Do you wanna bend her neck too?

1109
00:46:38,300 --> 00:46:39,700
- [LAUGHTER]
- Please, don't.

1110
00:46:39,700 --> 00:46:41,200
Then I'll put ketchup.
Just kidding.

1111
00:46:41,200 --> 00:46:42,933
- Then, um...
- Do you eat

1112
00:46:42,933 --> 00:46:44,133
<i> Sinigang</i> with her head.

1113
00:46:44,167 --> 00:46:45,333
- [LAUGHTER]
- With the salmon's head.

1114
00:46:45,333 --> 00:46:47,467
[LAUGHS] I'm just kidding!

1115
00:46:47,467 --> 00:46:49,567
- Are you serious? With lime?
- Yes!

1116
00:46:49,567 --> 00:46:52,533
We're so used to spaghetti
cooked in Filipino style.

1117
00:46:52,533 --> 00:46:56,067
- My supporters get this.
- [AUDIENCE CHEERING]

1118
00:46:56,067 --> 00:46:57,300
You guys know too much.

1119
00:46:57,300 --> 00:46:59,900
Yeah, this weird food combo.

1120
00:47:00,667 --> 00:47:04,467
Unlike the typical way,
I eat spaghetti with lime.

1121
00:47:04,867 --> 00:47:06,333
This is my childhood.

1122
00:47:07,233 --> 00:47:09,833
When I was a kid,
this was what I liked to eat.

1123
00:47:09,833 --> 00:47:12,100
Who influenced this?
Who started this?

1124
00:47:12,100 --> 00:47:14,267
- Me.
- Who influenced you to do this?

1125
00:47:14,267 --> 00:47:16,167
It was just me.
I really like sour food.

1126
00:47:16,200 --> 00:47:18,100
Then I thought about how
Filipino spaghetti is sweet,

1127
00:47:18,800 --> 00:47:22,233
So, why not--
I actually like lime.

1128
00:47:22,233 --> 00:47:24,267
It's sweet and sour,
so that's the combo.

1129
00:47:25,100 --> 00:47:28,767
Why don't we add groupers to
it if you want sweet and sour?

1130
00:47:28,767 --> 00:47:30,567
How does it taste?

1131
00:47:30,567 --> 00:47:33,067
- Don't speak in English.
- [SILLY SFX PLAYING]

1132
00:47:33,067 --> 00:47:36,100
Speaking in Kapampangan
doesn't suit you as well.

1133
00:47:36,100 --> 00:47:38,233
- It's good.
- Is it?

1134
00:47:38,233 --> 00:47:39,267
Not that.

1135
00:47:39,767 --> 00:47:41,233
- That's my brush.
- [LAUGHTER]

1136
00:47:41,233 --> 00:47:43,433
- That's for the spaghetti!
- [UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

1137
00:47:43,433 --> 00:47:45,300
[TETAY] That's
for the spaghetti!

1138
00:47:45,300 --> 00:47:47,600
[VICE] Wait! There's
sauce in it! Oh my God!

1139
00:47:47,600 --> 00:47:49,167
- I thought it was clean!
- [TETAY] It's clean!

1140
00:47:49,167 --> 00:47:51,400
- [VERNA LAUGHS]
- There's sauce!

1141
00:47:51,433 --> 00:47:53,200
You used it as a hairbrush!

1142
00:47:53,200 --> 00:47:54,933
- [LAUGH TRACK PLAYING]
- Aw.

1143
00:47:55,500 --> 00:47:57,467
Aw!

1144
00:47:58,700 --> 00:48:00,100
- Aw!
- Aw!

1145
00:48:00,100 --> 00:48:01,167
- [MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]
- Aw!

1146
00:48:01,167 --> 00:48:02,667
- You look like a Tamagotchi.
- [LAUGHTER]

1147
00:48:02,667 --> 00:48:04,900
- [UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]
- The virtual pet from before.

1148
00:48:04,900 --> 00:48:07,967
Meme is acting like that,
but she's secretly swooning.

1149
00:48:07,967 --> 00:48:10,033
- Who?
- [TETAY] You!

1150
00:48:10,033 --> 00:48:12,200
- But...
- I'm already married.

1151
00:48:12,200 --> 00:48:14,467
- Ion and I are friends.
- They're actually friends.

1152
00:48:14,467 --> 00:48:16,633
We play basketball together.

1153
00:48:16,633 --> 00:48:18,767
Who wouldn't swoon
when it comes to Alden?

1154
00:48:18,767 --> 00:48:20,200
It's Alden Richards

1155
00:48:20,200 --> 00:48:22,600
- Jose Rizal didn't swoon.
- [LAUGHTER]

1156
00:48:22,600 --> 00:48:24,133
He wasn't there!

1157
00:48:24,167 --> 00:48:25,533
Do you really think
Jose Rizal would swoon?!

1158
00:48:25,533 --> 00:48:27,967
- Taste the spaghetti!
- Just taste the spaghetti!

1159
00:48:27,967 --> 00:48:29,867
- I'll taste it.
- Yeah, sure.

1160
00:48:29,867 --> 00:48:33,200
It's not that different
since we have sour pastas.

1161
00:48:33,200 --> 00:48:35,833
How much lime do you put?

1162
00:48:35,833 --> 00:48:37,533
There's only two there, Vice.

1163
00:48:39,000 --> 00:48:40,967
- But it tastes fine.
- [VERNA] Does it taste good?

1164
00:48:40,967 --> 00:48:42,700
[LAUGHTER]

1165
00:48:42,700 --> 00:48:44,767
- Does it taste weird?
- What do you think, Meme?

1166
00:48:44,767 --> 00:48:46,400
- [TETAY] Here you go, Verna.
- [ALDEN] Weird?

1167
00:48:46,400 --> 00:48:47,833
- You know what...
- [TETAY] Be honest.

1168
00:48:48,400 --> 00:48:50,100
Alden is such a good sport.

1169
00:48:50,367 --> 00:48:51,567
He's so down to earth.

1170
00:48:52,033 --> 00:48:56,400
But the spaghetti
is just so cold.

1171
00:48:56,400 --> 00:48:58,133
[LAUGHTER]

1172
00:48:58,167 --> 00:49:00,600
Why is this so cold?!

1173
00:49:00,600 --> 00:49:02,933
There's ice cream underneath!

1174
00:49:04,000 --> 00:49:06,300
- You didn't say anything.
- It was the ice creams fault.

1175
00:49:06,300 --> 00:49:07,267
Okay, let's--

1176
00:49:07,267 --> 00:49:10,233
Even without the lime,
it's already sour!

1177
00:49:10,233 --> 00:49:12,500
- I think it's spoiled.
- It's already spoiled.

1178
00:49:12,500 --> 00:49:14,667
- [SILLY SFX PLAYING]
- Is this not Italian pasta?

1179
00:49:14,667 --> 00:49:17,833
What's funny
is that Alden ate a lot,

1180
00:49:17,833 --> 00:49:20,233
and he acted like it was good.

1181
00:49:20,233 --> 00:49:22,000
He's such a commercial model.

1182
00:49:22,000 --> 00:49:24,000
- [LAUGHS] I stuck with it.
- He's such an endorser.

1183
00:49:24,000 --> 00:49:26,600
- Endorser.
- [LAUGH TRACK PLAYING]

1184
00:49:26,600 --> 00:49:28,367
- Okay.
- There's one more thing.

1185
00:49:28,367 --> 00:49:29,500
What else do you need?

1186
00:49:29,500 --> 00:49:31,500
- Ketchup.
- For spaghetti too?

1187
00:49:31,533 --> 00:49:32,933
No, for noodles!

1188
00:49:34,767 --> 00:49:37,200
- But--
- Why put it with noodles?

1189
00:49:37,200 --> 00:49:43,133
I discovered this
when I was young too.

1190
00:49:43,133 --> 00:49:44,433
I was a bit of a--

1191
00:49:44,433 --> 00:49:46,533
You discovered a lot of things
as a kid. Are you a scientist?

1192
00:49:46,533 --> 00:49:47,833
- [LAUGHTER]
- [SILLY SFX PLAYING]

1193
