Santa Rosa</i> was in season.

1426
00:59:09,900 --> 00:59:13,100
Our town captain
forced me to do that.

1427
00:59:13,100 --> 00:59:14,400
- So I had no choice.
- Did you win again?

1428
00:59:14,600 --> 00:59:16,000
Yes, it felt good.

1429
00:59:16,000 --> 00:59:17,600
I won 70,000 pesos.

1430
00:59:17,600 --> 00:59:19,733
- Oh, really?
- Yeah!

1431
00:59:19,733 --> 00:59:22,733
That was my first time
having 70,000.

1432
00:59:22,733 --> 00:59:25,133
- So the first thing I did--
- That's a lot of money already!

1433
00:59:25,133 --> 00:59:27,233
The first thing I did
was go to the bank.

1434
00:59:27,233 --> 00:59:30,200
I didn't know what to do.
I just followed my grandma.

1435
00:59:30,200 --> 00:59:32,100
I actually grew up
around my grandma, Vice.

1436
00:59:32,133 --> 00:59:36,667
She taught me
that every penny counts.

1437
00:59:36,667 --> 00:59:42,333
She told me that I should
spend with intention.

1438
00:59:42,333 --> 00:59:44,033
When did you begin
working as an actor?

1439
00:59:44,033 --> 00:59:46,533
How did you get into acting?

1440
00:59:46,533 --> 00:59:50,500
After I joined<i> Ginoong Laguna,
</i>that's when...

1441
00:59:50,500 --> 00:59:52,367
- [VICE] Someone discovered you?
- Yes, someone did.

1442
00:59:52,367 --> 00:59:55,200
It was Carlites De Guzman.
My fans know him too.

1443
00:59:55,200 --> 00:59:56,600
Right?

1444
00:59:56,600 --> 00:59:58,733
- [VICE] He was your manager.
- Yes, until now.

1445
00:59:58,733 --> 01:00:00,433
- Ah, really?
- Actually, uh...

1446
01:00:00,433 --> 01:00:02,700
- We have no contract.
- Oh!

1447
01:00:02,700 --> 01:00:03,833
We don't have a contract,

1448
01:00:03,833 --> 01:00:06,167
but the recognition and, ah...

1449
01:00:06,200 --> 01:00:09,500
everything is mine.

1450
01:00:09,500 --> 01:00:10,767
There's no need for papers.

1451
01:00:10,767 --> 01:00:12,867
There are a lot of talent
managers like that.

1452
01:00:12,867 --> 01:00:16,200
You have an
artist-manager relationship,

1453
01:00:16,200 --> 01:00:17,533
but they have no contract
binding them.

1454
01:00:17,533 --> 01:00:18,967
But they work together.

1455
01:00:18,967 --> 01:00:21,800
There are those who
have a contract binding them,

1456
01:00:21,800 --> 01:00:24,900
- but they don't get projects.
- Yes. [LAUGHS]

1457
01:00:25,333 --> 01:00:26,467
What is that?

1458
01:00:26,833 --> 01:00:29,133
That's what hurts, right?

1459
01:00:29,133 --> 01:00:30,733
You don't have a contract
with your manager,

1460
01:00:30,733 --> 01:00:32,267
but you have tons of projects.

1461
01:00:32,267 --> 01:00:34,367
Others have a contract
with their managers,

1462
01:00:34,367 --> 01:00:35,633
you have waited
a long time to sign,

1463
01:00:35,633 --> 01:00:37,267
but not a single project
came in for you.

1464
01:00:37,300 --> 01:00:38,433
Oh!

1465
01:00:38,433 --> 01:00:40,400
- That's true.
- It's painful, right?

1466
01:00:40,400 --> 01:00:41,967
Gosh, when am I going to be
free from this?

1467
01:00:41,967 --> 01:00:44,100
I signed ages ago, but I still
haven't gotten any projects yet.

1468
01:00:44,100 --> 01:00:45,267
- Good for you.
- 20 years.

1469
01:00:45,267 --> 01:00:47,200
- No contracts!
- None! But...

1470
01:00:47,200 --> 01:00:52,633
One of the things that I admire
about Miss Carlites is

1471
01:00:52,633 --> 01:00:54,800
she never showed up here.

1472
01:00:54,800 --> 01:00:56,500
GMA knows this.

1473
01:00:56,500 --> 01:00:59,267
Carlites has never
set foot in GMA.

1474
01:00:59,267 --> 01:01:00,233
Why?

1475
01:01:00,233 --> 01:01:01,700
- Uh...
- Is she part of a syndicate?

1476
01:01:01,700 --> 01:01:02,867
Why isn't she showing herself?

1477
01:01:02,867 --> 01:01:04,067
I'm starting to think that too.

1478
01:01:04,067 --> 01:01:07,133
Does she have an estafa case?
Was she a scammer before?

1479
01:01:07,133 --> 01:01:08,767
Not like that. Like...

1480
01:01:08,767 --> 01:01:10,567
Maybe we're like...

1481
01:01:10,600 --> 01:01:12,567
She doesn't make
her presence felt always?

1482
01:01:12,567 --> 01:01:15,600
She's not like,
sorry for lack of a better term,

1483
01:01:15,600 --> 01:01:17,567
she doesn't like to show-off.

1484
01:01:17,567 --> 01:01:18,767
No, she's not like that.

1485
01:01:18,767 --> 01:01:21,333
Managers who like to be known
as much as their talents.

1486
01:01:21,333 --> 01:01:24,267
There's no such thing for us.
And I'm the only one...

1487
01:01:24,267 --> 01:01:26,933
She also handles other talents

1488
01:01:26,933 --> 01:01:29,100
but I'm the only one who

1489
01:01:29,100 --> 01:01:31,933
reached this level
in terms of career.

1490
01:01:31,933 --> 01:01:34,267
Were you in college
when you became an actor

1491
01:01:34,267 --> 01:01:35,467
or have you graduated already?

1492
01:01:35,467 --> 01:01:36,567
I was in college.

1493
01:01:36,567 --> 01:01:38,833
Is this your dream as a child or

1494
01:01:38,833 --> 01:01:40,600
you never thought
you'd be an actor?

1495
01:01:40,600 --> 01:01:41,600
- You didn't want to?
- I didn't want to.

1496
01:01:41,600 --> 01:01:42,867
I really don't want to.

1497
01:01:42,867 --> 01:01:45,467
I didn't have confidence
in myself before. And then,

1498
01:01:45,500 --> 01:01:48,000
I started gaining
a bit of confidence

1499
01:01:48,000 --> 01:01:49,333
when I joined pageants.

1500
01:01:49,333 --> 01:01:51,600
But it never crossed my mind

1501
01:01:51,600 --> 01:01:53,533
that I would be able
to get into this industry.

1502
01:01:53,533 --> 01:01:57,367
Because the people in
this industry are good looking.

1503
01:01:58,133 --> 01:01:59,600
Yes. That's exactly
what we were.

1504
01:01:59,600 --> 01:02:00,833
When you entered the industry,

1505
01:02:00,833 --> 01:02:02,100
that's how we were.

1506
01:02:02,100 --> 01:02:03,367
Yes! Ouch!

1507
01:02:04,133 --> 01:02:05,200
Sorry. Sorry.

1508
01:02:05,200 --> 01:02:07,333
I'm sorry, you had
a hard time reaching my...

1509
01:02:07,333 --> 01:02:09,333
- [LAUGHS]
- our standard. [LAUGHS]

1510
01:02:09,333 --> 01:02:11,000
Just kidding! But before,

1511
01:02:11,000 --> 01:02:13,500
when you were
starting out in the industry

1512
01:02:13,500 --> 01:02:15,267
who's the artist you
wanted to work with?

1513
01:02:15,267 --> 01:02:17,400
What show were you always
watching before?

1514
01:02:17,400 --> 01:02:19,667
Not me! My mother!

1515
01:02:19,700 --> 01:02:21,367
What show did she watch before?

1516
01:02:21,367 --> 01:02:25,767
<i> Marimar!
</i>When I was in grade six,

1517
01:02:25,767 --> 01:02:28,767
she was always the one who...

1518
01:02:28,767 --> 01:02:32,767
Because she is a big fan
of Filipino teleseryes

1519
01:02:32,767 --> 01:02:35,067
and Mexican telenovelas.

1520
01:02:35,067 --> 01:02:37,567
That would be around 2000s.

1521
01:02:37,567 --> 01:02:39,167
They're being shown
in the afternoon!

1522
01:02:39,167 --> 01:02:40,867
They go alongside
the 3 o'clock prayer.

1523
01:02:40,867 --> 01:02:45,167
Yes! After doing the laundry,
cooking lunch

1524
01:02:45,167 --> 01:02:47,233
that would last until dinner.
That's what she'd watch.

1525
01:02:47,233 --> 01:02:48,900
Yes! The telenovelas
will be shown first.

1526
01:02:48,900 --> 01:02:52,733
You're going to see
Marimar and Sergio!

1527
01:02:52,767 --> 01:02:55,400
They're kissing!

1528
01:02:55,400 --> 01:02:56,533
Then suddenly,
there's a commercial.

1529
01:02:56,533 --> 01:02:59,400
"Holy God. Holy Mighty One.
Holy Immortal One.

1530
01:02:59,400 --> 01:03:00,700
- 3 o'clock prayer!
- Have mercy on us

1531
01:03:00,700 --> 01:03:02,767
and on the whole word.
Holy God..."

1532
01:03:02,767 --> 01:03:04,633
Yes! Right after.

1533
01:03:04,633 --> 01:03:07,967
There'll be kissing then right
after, there's Sister Faustina.

1534
01:03:07,967 --> 01:03:09,300
What's going on?

1535
01:03:09,300 --> 01:03:12,933
- The segue is insane!
- The sequence is so wrong!

1536
01:03:12,933 --> 01:03:15,033
- But it's really<i> Marimar.
</i>- Yes!

1537
01:03:15,033 --> 01:03:16,633
At the time, my mother said,

1538
01:03:16,633 --> 01:03:19,633
- "Tisoy." She was really...
- [DISTANT LAUGHING]

1539
01:03:19,633 --> 01:03:21,833
[VICE] Why are you
laughing there?

1540
01:03:21,833 --> 01:03:23,933
Because what you said is true!

1541
01:03:23,933 --> 01:03:26,067
Sergio's being shown, suddenly
the prayer would start after.

1542
01:03:26,100 --> 01:03:27,667
- Oh, come on!
- Right after the kissing scene!

1543
01:03:27,667 --> 01:03:30,800
Your "Oh, Sergio" will turn into

1544
01:03:30,800 --> 01:03:32,400
"Oh, let's pray first."

1545
01:03:32,400 --> 01:03:36,067
[VICE] Sergio's being shown
wearing trunks...

1546
01:03:36,067 --> 01:03:39,033
[SEDUCTIVELY] Then
you're like "Sergio, Sergio!"

1547
01:03:39,033 --> 01:03:40,267
[ALDEN] Then suddenly,
"Holy God..."

1548
01:03:40,267 --> 01:03:45,267
[LAUGHTER]

1549
01:03:46,767 --> 01:03:51,000
Sometimes, the programming is
not being planned and it shows.

1550
01:03:51,000 --> 01:03:53,900
So, it was your mother's dream?

1551
01:03:53,900 --> 01:03:56,733
It was her dream that
when you became an actor,

1552
01:03:56,733 --> 01:03:58,633
- you can take roles like that.
- Yes! On that level.

1553
01:03:58,667 --> 01:04:00,667
She hopes that I'd be
a knight in shining armor

1554
01:04:00,667 --> 01:04:02,500
of a damsel in distress.

1555
01:04:02,933 --> 01:04:05,467
- Riding a horse!
- Oh my!

1556
01:04:05,467 --> 01:04:06,700
You didn't tell me you

1557
01:04:06,700 --> 01:04:08,967
- wanted to work with me!
- I said the wrong thing!

1558
01:04:08,967 --> 01:04:11,000
This is really where
you'd share that, huh?

1559
01:04:11,000 --> 01:04:12,067
Sorry, sorry!

1560
01:04:12,067 --> 01:04:13,900
You even talked about
a damsel in distress

1561
01:04:13,900 --> 01:04:15,667
when you just
want to ride a horse!

1562
01:04:16,500 --> 01:04:19,267
- You have a foul mouth!
- [DIVINE] He just said sorry!

1563
01:04:19,267 --> 01:04:22,067
Your mouth! [LAUGHS]

1564
01:04:22,067 --> 01:04:23,600
But...

1565
01:04:23,600 --> 01:04:26,767
Wasn't there a GMA
adaptation of Marimar?

1566
01:04:26,767 --> 01:04:29,867
[ALDEN] It starred Marian Rivera
and Dingdong Dantes.

1567
01:04:29,867 --> 01:04:32,167
- And Megan Young.
- You didn't auditon for that?

1568
01:04:32,200 --> 01:04:33,733
They didn't recreate it.

1569
01:04:33,733 --> 01:04:36,800
When I became an actor,
it was already done.

1570
01:04:37,633 --> 01:04:39,767
- I auditioned in there.
- Wow!

1571
01:04:39,767 --> 01:04:41,633
- [ALDEN] Wow! As?
- [DIVINE] Really?

1572
01:04:41,633 --> 01:04:44,000
As Corazon,
but I didn't get picked.

1573
01:04:44,533 --> 01:04:46,333
You're not fit for the role.
You used glutathione.

1574
01:04:46,333 --> 01:04:49,267
- [VERNA] Ah, Corazon?
- I'm not fit.

1575
01:04:49,267 --> 01:04:53,067
Who was your first crush in GMA?

1576
01:04:54,767 --> 01:04:55,900
[AUDIENCE] Yiee.

1577
01:04:55,900 --> 01:04:59,267
First showbiz crush,
not just in GMA.

1578
01:04:59,267 --> 01:05:01,567
- In showbiz, in general?
- Anne Curtis.

1579
01:05:01,567 --> 01:05:03,333
- Ah.
- Anne Curtis, really.

1580
01:05:03,333 --> 01:05:04,833
I don't get it. Why?

1581
01:05:04,867 --> 01:05:06,700
- Ah!
- [LAUGHTER]

1582
01:05:06,700 --> 01:05:10,167
I just can't see anything
so special about that girl.

1583
01:05:10,167 --> 01:05:11,833
She's so basic.

1584
01:05:11,833 --> 01:05:13,433
- I mean...
- [LAUGHTER]

1585
01:05:13,433 --> 01:05:15,500
- [DIVINE] You don't get it!
- Yes, yes, yes.

1586
01:05:15,500 --> 01:05:18,733
I've been with her, like,
almost everyday for the past

1587
01:05:18,733 --> 01:05:19,833
- 16 years.
- [ALDEN] Yes.

1588
01:05:19,833 --> 01:05:23,000
And I just don't see
anything special about her.

1589
01:05:23,000 --> 01:05:26,633
Yes. For me, she's someone
you can just, you know,

1590
01:05:26,633 --> 01:05:28,067
bump into...

1591
01:05:28,067 --> 01:05:29,567
[ALDEN] In public places.

1592
01:05:29,567 --> 01:05:32,333
Yes. In MRT, LRT, like that.

1593
01:05:32,333 --> 01:05:34,233
What is it about Anne Curtis?

1594
01:05:34,233 --> 01:05:37,133
Aside from being able
to eat a shoe that big.

1595
01:05:37,133 --> 01:05:38,900
- Eat?
- Yes.

1596
01:05:39,767 --> 01:05:42,200
That's her superpower!
Her mouth is so big!

1597
01:05:42,200 --> 01:05:43,833
- Oh my god.
- Yes!

1598
01:05:43,833 --> 01:05:46,133
You can even hide
a suitcase in her mouth!

1599
01:05:46,133 --> 01:05:48,500
Hand carry? No! Uh...

1600
01:05:48,500 --> 01:05:51,867
No, uh...

1601
01:05:51,867 --> 01:05:55,333
Normally, the first
means of attraction

1602
01:05:55,333 --> 01:05:57,500
comes from
the physical, right? Like...

1603
01:05:57,500 --> 01:05:58,833
You're looking
at me differently!

1604
01:05:58,833 --> 01:06:00,200
Don't mention me. Anyway!

1605
01:06:00,200 --> 01:06:02,600
[ALDEN LAUGHS] Physical, right?

1606
01:06:02,600 --> 01:06:04,000
- Like...
- Yes.

1607
01:06:04,000 --> 01:06:05,567
He said physical. Verna...

1608
01:06:05,567 --> 01:06:07,567
- Oh, I'm in.
- Yes.

1609
01:06:07,567 --> 01:06:09,133
Fish... Fish-ical.

1610
01:06:09,767 --> 01:06:12,067
- [ALDEN] A fish?
- A fish!

1611
01:06:12,500 --> 01:06:15,300
So, yeah. She's unique.

1612
01:06:15,300 --> 01:06:20,033
Anne's physicality was
very unique during that time.

1613
01:06:20,033 --> 01:06:22,067
I even used to call her
<i> Ate</i> (older sister).

1614
01:06:22,067 --> 01:06:23,233
- Yes.
- Yes.

1615
01:06:23,233 --> 01:06:25,167
So that's it.
And then, I'll never forget,

1616
01:06:25,167 --> 01:06:30,200
the first time we met
was in a school in Ortigas.

1617
01:06:30,200 --> 01:06:31,333
She had a full bangs back then

1618
01:06:31,333 --> 01:06:34,633
and she rode in
a compact orange car.

1619
01:06:34,633 --> 01:06:35,967
I won't mention the car's brand.

1620
01:06:35,967 --> 01:06:38,133
No, Anne Curtis has
a beautiful aura.

1621
01:06:38,133 --> 01:06:39,400
- Yes.
- Right?

1622
01:06:39,400 --> 01:06:41,867
It's very positive.

1623
01:06:41,867 --> 01:06:43,733
You'll feel a different kind
of warmth

1624
01:06:43,733 --> 01:06:45,133
when you're in the presence
of Anne Curtis.

1625
01:06:45,167 --> 01:06:47,067
- [DIVINE] Her energy!
- She has good energy.

1626
01:06:47,067 --> 01:06:49,167
- She has good vibes.
- Like Verna, Vice?

1627
01:06:49,167 --> 01:06:50,367
- Who?
- The energy?

1628
01:06:50,367 --> 01:06:52,333
Verna is pretty!
She just cremated alive

1629
01:06:52,333 --> 01:06:54,233
that's why she looked like that.

1630
01:06:54,233 --> 01:06:57,467
Alden, don't compare me to her.

1631
01:06:57,467 --> 01:06:59,500
[VICE, ALDEN] Why?

1632
01:06:59,500 --> 01:07:01,767
- I'm better.
- [DIVINE] You know,

1633
01:07:01,767 --> 01:07:05,067
Alden has this gift where

1634
01:07:05,067 --> 01:07:08,300
when there is
an exchange in dialogue,

1635
01:07:08,300 --> 01:07:10,867
he will make you feel...

1636
01:07:10,867 --> 01:07:13,200
- You're acting like a couple,
- [VICE] If you're his co-actor,

1637
01:07:13,200 --> 01:07:15,967
I've heard lots of things
like that from his co-actors,

1638
01:07:15,967 --> 01:07:18,333
that if you're in a scene with
him, the scene will feel real.

1639
01:07:18,367 --> 01:07:22,700
Yes! Especially when
he looks at you,

1640
01:07:22,700 --> 01:07:24,900
you'll be like,
"There you go again."

1641
01:07:24,900 --> 01:07:27,633
"We both feel the same way."
[LAUGHS]

1642
01:07:27,633 --> 01:07:30,000
Right? Oh, look at Verna.

1643
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:31,200
See?

1644
01:07:31,533 --> 01:07:33,967
I think the music
should be sensual.

1645
01:07:34,800 --> 01:07:36,067
I'm going to say something here.

1646
01:07:36,067 --> 01:07:37,333
Oh!

1647
01:07:37,333 --> 01:07:39,133
- [DIVINE] Give in!
- [VICE] Verna, come here!

1648
01:07:39,133 --> 01:07:41,000
- Come here!
- Go there!

1649
01:07:41,000 --> 01:07:43,733
I'm married so I can't do
things like this anymore.

1650
01:07:43,733 --> 01:07:46,367
Verna, come sit here.

1651
01:07:46,800 --> 01:07:50,067
Before anything, I'll inform you
that I'm married too.

1652
01:07:50,067 --> 01:07:51,767
You're not, for now. Oh!

1653
01:07:51,800 --> 01:07:53,333
[AUDIENCE SCREAMING, LAUGHING]

1654
01:07:53,333 --> 01:07:57,900
[VERNA LAUGHING]

1655
01:07:59,000 --> 01:08:00,033
Why isn't it...

1656
01:08:00,033 --> 01:08:02,500
It seems like there's
something stopping us

1657
01:08:02,500 --> 01:08:03,733
from doing
what we are about to do.

1658
01:08:03,733 --> 01:08:04,867
I agree!

1659
01:08:04,867 --> 01:08:06,900
I already fell and
you didn't even catch me!

1660
01:08:06,900 --> 01:08:08,633
Hey!

1661
01:08:08,700 --> 01:08:11,900
What would you say to the women
who fantasizes about Alden?

1662
01:08:11,900 --> 01:08:16,100
- Sorry!
- [LAUGHTER]

1663
01:08:16,100 --> 01:08:18,967
- You all lost to Verna!
- [LAUGHTER]

