01:25:23,467 --> 01:25:26,033
[VICE] Wow, you have
a location manager...

2136
01:25:26,033 --> 01:25:29,300
- [LAUGHTER]
- ...for public restrooms!

2137
01:25:29,300 --> 01:25:32,133
He'd be like, "Please check."
And they'd say, "Alden, clear."

2138
01:25:32,133 --> 01:25:35,167
- [LAUGHTER]
- That's what Mama Ten does!

2139
01:25:35,167 --> 01:25:37,900
Since she has motion sickness...

2140
01:25:37,900 --> 01:25:40,533
Isn't it obvious?
Just kidding.

2141
01:25:41,633 --> 01:25:44,500
So, she'd go first
while I wait in the car.

2142
01:25:44,500 --> 01:25:47,000
She'd check the restrooms first.

2143
01:25:47,000 --> 01:25:48,867
But this time,
I couldn't hold it in,

2144
01:25:48,867 --> 01:25:50,300
so I called her to hurry up.

2145
01:25:50,300 --> 01:25:52,367
If you think actors are perfect,
you're wrong.

2146
01:25:52,367 --> 01:25:56,400
We have disgusting sides too.
And we can't help it.

2147
01:25:56,400 --> 01:25:59,700
But going back to my story
about that farm in Rizal...

2148
01:25:59,700 --> 01:26:02,333
So, I went inside the hut.

2149
01:26:02,333 --> 01:26:05,233
It looked decent enough.

2150
01:26:05,233 --> 01:26:08,100
The restroom was closed off.

2151
01:26:08,100 --> 01:26:09,400
So, I went inside.

2152
01:26:10,400 --> 01:26:14,300
When I entered the restroom,
I was like, "Ma, is this it?"

2153
01:26:14,333 --> 01:26:16,533
She said yes,
so I was like, "Where?"

2154
01:26:16,533 --> 01:26:21,133
Because all I saw
was a small hole in the ground.

2155
01:26:21,933 --> 01:26:23,767
[VICE] What an experience.

2156
01:26:23,767 --> 01:26:25,900
Have you told that story
to your previous girlfriends?

2157
01:26:27,000 --> 01:26:30,000
- No.
- [VICE LAUGHS]

2158
01:26:30,000 --> 01:26:32,667
You kept it from your
previous girlfriends,

2159
01:26:32,667 --> 01:26:36,000
but you shared it with
so many people tonight.

2160
01:26:36,000 --> 01:26:37,333
How many girlfriends
have you had?

2161
01:26:38,100 --> 01:26:41,333
With proper label, only two.

2162
01:26:41,933 --> 01:26:43,467
- Just two.
- How old are you?

2163
01:26:43,467 --> 01:26:44,600
Thirty-four.

2164
01:26:44,600 --> 01:26:46,300
Just two? Did they last?

2165
01:26:46,333 --> 01:26:47,733
It happened
back in high school.

2166
01:26:47,733 --> 01:26:49,367
[VICE] Non-showbiz?

2167
01:26:49,367 --> 01:26:52,000
All the relationships I've had
since I entered showbiz...

2168
01:26:52,700 --> 01:26:55,867
None of them became official.

2169
01:26:55,867 --> 01:26:58,733
I'd connect with them,
but nothing came of it.

2170
01:26:58,733 --> 01:27:01,233
- Maybe it's not meant for me.
- [VICE] You mean...

2171
01:27:01,233 --> 01:27:04,133
...almost-but-not-quite
relationships?

2172
01:27:04,133 --> 01:27:06,633
None of them became official.
I don't know why.

2173
01:27:06,633 --> 01:27:08,633
I don't want to
name names anymore.

2174
01:27:08,633 --> 01:27:11,633
You've already heard it
on the news anyway.

2175
01:27:11,633 --> 01:27:15,733
I won't mention their names
and bother them anymore.

2176
01:27:15,733 --> 01:27:16,900
[VICE] Aww.

2177
01:27:16,900 --> 01:27:19,900
- You fell in love with them?
- Of course. Yes.

2178
01:27:19,933 --> 01:27:22,100
How many women have you
been involved with in showbiz?

2179
01:27:22,100 --> 01:27:24,200
- Five.
- Oh, five?

2180
01:27:24,200 --> 01:27:27,433
- Five situationships?
- Yes.

2181
01:27:27,433 --> 01:27:29,633
Why do you think
none of them worked out?

2182
01:27:30,867 --> 01:27:32,433
I don't know either.

2183
01:27:32,433 --> 01:27:35,000
Maybe I'm the problem.

2184
01:27:35,000 --> 01:27:37,767
- Maybe--
- Who breaks it off?

2185
01:27:39,133 --> 01:27:41,533
Sometimes, me.
Sometimes, the other party.

2186
01:27:41,533 --> 01:27:43,400
But the last one,
she broke it off.

2187
01:27:45,000 --> 01:27:46,333
Shit. Sorry.

2188
01:27:46,333 --> 01:27:47,867
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER
FROM AUDIENCE]

2189
01:27:47,867 --> 01:27:49,967
Your eyes changed.

2190
01:27:49,967 --> 01:27:52,000
The last one...

2191
01:27:52,000 --> 01:27:53,500
[VICE] She pulled back?

2192
01:27:53,533 --> 01:27:55,833
We both did,
but it's more on her.

2193
01:27:56,567 --> 01:27:57,567
Why?

2194
01:27:59,300 --> 01:28:01,133
I think, um...

2195
01:28:01,133 --> 01:28:03,233
[VICE]
I'm so curious. Wait.

2196
01:28:03,233 --> 01:28:04,333
[LAUGHTER]

2197
01:28:04,333 --> 01:28:07,333
I wanna be in the know.
Come closer. [CHUCKLES]

2198
01:28:07,333 --> 01:28:10,700
Why did she break it off?
What was her reason?

2199
01:28:10,700 --> 01:28:13,700
Cris! Vice is asking
too many questions!

2200
01:28:13,700 --> 01:28:15,033
No, um...

2201
01:28:15,033 --> 01:28:16,067
How do I explain it?

2202
01:28:16,767 --> 01:28:17,800
Uh...

2203
01:28:19,067 --> 01:28:22,733
It's hard. I feel like it's not
my piece to say.

2204
01:28:22,733 --> 01:28:25,367
- I shouldn't speak for her.
- Okay, just tell us your side.

2205
01:28:25,400 --> 01:28:27,367
What's the reason
you pulled back?

2206
01:28:27,367 --> 01:28:29,533
You said you both pulled back.

2207
01:28:29,533 --> 01:28:31,633
But what was your reason?

2208
01:28:32,400 --> 01:28:37,633
I think what I learned
from my experience

2209
01:28:37,633 --> 01:28:40,800
with that relationship
is never say never.

2210
01:28:40,800 --> 01:28:43,333
Don't give yourself
an ultimatum

2211
01:28:43,333 --> 01:28:45,500
because you're too
happy with the situation.

2212
01:28:46,733 --> 01:28:48,667
I ate my words.

2213
01:28:50,333 --> 01:28:52,133
- And--
- Then, you had to poo.

2214
01:28:52,133 --> 01:28:54,100
- Yeah.
- [LAUGHTER]

2215
01:28:54,100 --> 01:28:55,867
I had to go straight
to the toilet.

2216
01:28:55,867 --> 01:28:57,700
- Yeah.
- He had to pull back

2217
01:28:57,700 --> 01:29:01,000
because had to go
take a dump at the gas station.

2218
01:29:01,033 --> 01:29:03,867
- Because I ate my words.
- [LAUGHS]

2219
01:29:03,867 --> 01:29:05,367
I guess it just happened.

2220
01:29:05,367 --> 01:29:08,567
You also said there were times
when it was you who pulled back.

2221
01:29:08,567 --> 01:29:10,733
- Yes.
- How do you say that...

2222
01:29:10,733 --> 01:29:12,100
to a woman that...

2223
01:29:13,400 --> 01:29:15,100
...you no longer want
that relationship?

2224
01:29:15,100 --> 01:29:17,000
Do you just walk away?

2225
01:29:17,000 --> 01:29:19,833
For the first one,
I walked away without a word.

2226
01:29:19,833 --> 01:29:22,600
- I ghosted her. Mm-hmm.
- [VICE] Oh...

2227
01:29:22,600 --> 01:29:25,067
Which is not...

2228
01:29:25,067 --> 01:29:26,433
Uh...

2229
01:29:26,433 --> 01:29:27,467
Not good.

2230
01:29:27,467 --> 01:29:29,400
[VICE] Verna's okay
with being ghosted.

2231
01:29:29,400 --> 01:29:33,100
- Oh? But I thought--
- It's fine. I'll cling to you.

2232
01:29:33,133 --> 01:29:34,567
I thought you were the ghost.

2233
01:29:34,567 --> 01:29:37,533
- I'm kidding. I'm kidding.
- Her real name is Casper.

2234
01:29:37,533 --> 01:29:38,933
[LAUGHTER]

2235
01:29:38,933 --> 01:29:42,267
So, what about the rest
if you ghosted the first one?

2236
01:29:42,267 --> 01:29:44,433
You talked before you left?

2237
01:29:45,433 --> 01:29:48,433
Yes, we talked.
I mean, you know...

2238
01:29:48,433 --> 01:29:52,567
We learn from every circumstance
that happens in our lives.

2239
01:29:52,567 --> 01:29:54,467
But when it comes to love...

2240
01:29:54,467 --> 01:29:57,900
I feel like I've been
very unlucky with love

2241
01:29:57,900 --> 01:30:00,533
for the past 15 years

2242
01:30:00,533 --> 01:30:02,600
because I kept chasing it.

2243
01:30:02,600 --> 01:30:04,967
- [VICE] Ah.
- Because the fact that...

2244
01:30:04,967 --> 01:30:08,933
...I haven't started a family
at my age worries me.

2245
01:30:08,967 --> 01:30:11,867
- You feel pressured?
- Yes. That's how Pinoys are.

2246
01:30:11,867 --> 01:30:14,367
We live in a culture
of deadlines.

2247
01:30:14,367 --> 01:30:16,267
You have to be this or that
at a certain age.

2248
01:30:16,267 --> 01:30:20,267
But I don't think that's how I
want to live my life right now.

2249
01:30:20,267 --> 01:30:22,333
So, after the last one...

2250
01:30:23,433 --> 01:30:25,500
I decided to stop chasing love.

2251
01:30:25,500 --> 01:30:31,067
I'll live my life by accepting
whatever God sends my way,

2252
01:30:31,067 --> 01:30:33,900
may it be a circumstance,
a person...

2253
01:30:33,900 --> 01:30:35,800
I'm not saying I won't
fall in love anymore.

2254
01:30:35,800 --> 01:30:40,867
I'm not saying I've stopped
or I'm no longer waiting

2255
01:30:40,900 --> 01:30:42,900
for the right person to come.

2256
01:30:42,900 --> 01:30:46,700
Because for the longest time,
I actively searched for the one.

2257
01:30:46,700 --> 01:30:50,233
So maybe, for a change,
I should just wait for them.

2258
01:30:50,233 --> 01:30:55,400
You're just letting them
come your way.

2259
01:30:55,400 --> 01:30:59,000
You're no longer going out
of your way to meet them.

2260
01:30:59,000 --> 01:31:01,833
You're no longer trying
to find them.

2261
01:31:01,833 --> 01:31:05,433
I mean,
I already failed five times.

2262
01:31:05,433 --> 01:31:06,833
So, maybe I should
change gears.

2263
01:31:06,833 --> 01:31:08,600
[VICE] No, that's true.

2264
01:31:08,600 --> 01:31:11,200
Sometimes,
you really won't find it

2265
01:31:11,200 --> 01:31:13,333
if you actively keep
looking for it, right?

2266
01:31:13,367 --> 01:31:16,367
But when you just
leave it to fate,

2267
01:31:16,367 --> 01:31:18,200
it'll just surprise you.

2268
01:31:18,200 --> 01:31:21,000
It's like... It's like...

2269
01:31:21,000 --> 01:31:24,300
Like love is playing
hard to get.

2270
01:31:24,300 --> 01:31:25,767
When you want it,
you can't find it.

2271
01:31:25,767 --> 01:31:28,333
But when you let go,
it just finds you.

2272
01:31:28,333 --> 01:31:30,700
I'd compare it with...

2273
01:31:30,700 --> 01:31:32,733
It's like holding sand.

2274
01:31:33,467 --> 01:31:35,967
The more you try
to tighten your grip,

2275
01:31:35,967 --> 01:31:37,767
the more sand
escapes your fingers,

2276
01:31:37,767 --> 01:31:40,867
as opposed to just letting it
sit on your palm.

2277
01:31:40,867 --> 01:31:45,100
Somewhere out there,
I know that...

2278
01:31:45,100 --> 01:31:47,300
How many are we?

2279
01:31:47,333 --> 01:31:50,067
There are seven billion
people in the world.

2280
01:31:50,067 --> 01:31:51,800
I'm sure one of them
is meant for me.

2281
01:31:51,800 --> 01:31:53,967
- Yes.
- Aww!

2282
01:31:53,967 --> 01:31:57,067
For sure there's one person...

2283
01:31:57,933 --> 01:32:00,700
who will love and accept you
for who you are

2284
01:32:00,700 --> 01:32:04,933
and be brave enough
to fight for you.

2285
01:32:04,933 --> 01:32:06,400
That's so nice to hear.

2286
01:32:06,400 --> 01:32:08,600
So many people
can learn to love you.

2287
01:32:08,600 --> 01:32:10,967
And he can learn
to love them back.

2288
01:32:10,967 --> 01:32:13,933
But the question is,
will they fight for it?

2289
01:32:13,933 --> 01:32:16,467
Which one of them
will fight for your love?

2290
01:32:17,267 --> 01:32:18,300
Right?

2291
01:32:19,000 --> 01:32:23,000
And you'll be surprised.
When that person comes...

2292
01:32:24,167 --> 01:32:27,200
...she won't be
who you imagined her to be.

2293
01:32:28,533 --> 01:32:30,833
She won't be like you expected.

2294
01:32:30,833 --> 01:32:35,367
She won't be like you pictured
in your mind.

2295
01:32:35,367 --> 01:32:37,767
She may not even be
the one you asked for.

2296
01:32:39,200 --> 01:32:41,500
You might find
yourself thinking,

2297
01:32:41,500 --> 01:32:43,933
"You're not the one I asked for,

2298
01:32:43,933 --> 01:32:47,633
but you make me feel the love
that I've always longed for."

2299
01:32:47,633 --> 01:32:50,733
If it happens, It happens.

2300
01:32:50,733 --> 01:32:52,900
If it comes, it comes.

2301
01:32:52,933 --> 01:32:54,800
If it's there, it's there.

2302
01:32:56,033 --> 01:32:57,700
There's really
nothing you can do.

2303
01:32:57,700 --> 01:33:00,767
When it happens,
there's nothing you can do.

2304
01:33:00,767 --> 01:33:02,733
Because even if you want
something so badly,

2305
01:33:02,733 --> 01:33:05,500
if it's not the right time,
it won't work out.

2306
01:33:05,500 --> 01:33:08,267
I feel like that's what
has been happening.

2307
01:33:08,267 --> 01:33:13,533
And just like your iconic line
from your iconic TV segment,

2308
01:33:13,533 --> 01:33:15,467
"At the right time."

2309
01:33:15,467 --> 01:33:18,033
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

2310
01:33:18,033 --> 01:33:20,133
- Great.
- Yeah.

2311
01:33:20,133 --> 01:33:22,767
You may feel like relationships
aren't for you now.

2312
01:33:22,767 --> 01:33:26,533
Like complications always
arise whenever you find love.

2313
01:33:26,567 --> 01:33:28,200
And so you stop trying

2314
01:33:28,200 --> 01:33:31,467
because you think
you're better off without them.

2315
01:33:31,467 --> 01:33:34,567
But that's not true.
Genuine love feels so good.

2316
01:33:34,567 --> 01:33:36,433
Maybe it's also because...

2317
01:33:36,433 --> 01:33:42,267
For the longest time,
I've been trying to find love

2318
01:33:42,267 --> 01:33:44,367
from other people.

2319
01:33:45,667 --> 01:33:47,433
But I realized...

2320
01:33:49,067 --> 01:33:51,300
what I lacked was self-love.

2321
01:33:51,300 --> 01:33:54,100
[AUDIENCE] Aww!

2322
01:33:57,267 --> 01:33:59,400
<i> - Aww!
- Don't cry, Alden!</i>

2323
01:33:59,400 --> 01:34:01,467
<i>- It's okay!
- You'll be fine!</i>

2324
01:34:01,500 --> 01:34:08,367
[TENDER MUSIC PLAYING]

2325
01:34:22,500 --> 01:34:26,900
[TENDER MUSIC CONTINUES]

2326
01:34:26,900 --> 01:34:29,200
It took so long before I...

2327
01:34:36,267 --> 01:34:41,733
[BREATHING DEEPLY]

2328
01:34:45,667 --> 01:34:48,600
[VICE] I told you to come
only when you're called.

2329
01:34:48,600 --> 01:34:50,867
Where's her leash?!

2330
01:34:50,867 --> 01:34:54,833
[TETAY] She ate it because
no one gave her treats!

2331
01:34:54,833 --> 01:34:55,833
[VERNA CHUCKLES]

2332
01:34:55,833 --> 01:34:57,967
[TETAY] Aww! Tisoy!

2333
01:34:57,967 --> 01:34:59,967
[VICE] I... I understand.

2334
01:35:02,200 --> 01:35:04,467
Yeah. Believe me,
I understand.

2335
01:35:04,467 --> 01:35:05,967
I've been there.

2336
01:35:06,000 --> 01:35:07,167
[VERNA] Aww!

2337
01:35:07,167 --> 01:35:08,233
[VICE] Yeah.

2338
01:35:09,333 --> 01:35:11,833
And I know it's hard.

2339
01:35:11,833 --> 01:35:16,400
But at least now,
you're acknowledging it.

2340
01:35:16,400 --> 01:35:20,167
It's very important that
you acknowledge it.

2341
01:35:22,400 --> 01:35:25,733
Like, "Oh, maybe I should
find love for myself.

2342
01:35:25,733 --> 01:35:28,433
Because I kept looking for it
from other people

2343
01:35:28,433 --> 01:35:31,367
that I ended up forgetting
to love myself."

2344
01:35:31,367 --> 01:35:34,700
We keep longing
for someone else's love

2345
01:35:34,700 --> 01:35:38,133
that we sometimes forget
we can give that to ourselves.

2346
01:35:38,133 --> 01:35:41,133
And that love is
already inside us.

2347
01:35:44,833 --> 01:35:47,133
And because your heart
is very generous,

2348
01:35:47,133 --> 01:35:49,400
you have been giving so much
to the world.

2349
01:35:53,167 --> 01:36:00,033
[TENDER MUSIC CONTINUES]

2350
01:36:16,100 --> 01:36:23,033
[TENDER MUSIC CONTINUES]

2351
01:36:29,033 --> 01:36:31,900
[SOBBING]

2352
01:36:36,367 --> 01:36:38,800
I'm sorry, Vice.

2353
01:36:38,800 --> 01:36:45,433
[TENDER MUSIC CONTINUES]

2354
01:36:45,433 --> 01:36:50,067
Vice, I don't usually
let this out because...

2355
01:36:50,700 --> 01:36:53,567
[VICE] Sorry if there's
something we said

2356
01:36:53,567 --> 01:36:55,033
that triggered you.

2357
01:36:55,033 --> 01:36:58,500
No, actually, coming here,
I feel like...

2358
01:37:00,100 --> 01:37:03,133
this is the first time
I've really been able to say it.

2359
01:37:03,133 --> 01:37:04,500
[SNIFFLES]

2360
01:37:04,867 --> 01:37:09,600
All my life, I've just...
felt like...

2361
01:37:11,100 --> 01:37:16,533
[INAUDIBLE]

2362
01:37:16,533 --> 01:37:19,367
[SOBBING]

2363
01:37:21,933 --> 01:37:25,900
[TENDER MUSIC CONTINUES]

2364
01:37:25,900 --> 01:37:27,167
[VICE] We understand.

2365
01:37:27,167 --> 01:37:30,467
[ALDEN SOBBING]

2366
01:37:32,200 --> 01:37:33,500
I'm sorry.

2367
01:37:34,500 --> 01:37:39,133
[ALDEN SOBBING]

2368
01:37:42,733 --> 01:37:47,733
[TENDER MUSIC CONTINUES]

2369
01:37:49,333 --> 01:37:53,000
- [EXHALES DEEPLY]
- [VICE] Breathe.

2370
01:37:54,933 --> 01:37:56,067
[VICE] Breathe.

2371
01:37:58,300 --> 01:37:59,867
Breathe through your nose.

2372
01:38:01,233 --> 01:38:03,133
Hold... release.

2373
01:38:03,133 --> 01:38:07,133
[ALDEN BREATHES DEEPLY]

2374
01:38:10,933 --> 01:38:12,067
It's okay.

2375
01:38:14,367 --> 01:38:15,567
Sorry, guys.

2376
01:38:16,433 --> 01:38:18,833
[APPLAUSE]

2377
01:38:18,833 --> 01:38:25,533
[AUDIENCE CHEERING]

