01:57:52,833 --> 01:57:53,767
[LAUGHTER]

2869
01:57:53,800 --> 01:57:55,800
- This isn't Memerimar.
- [ALDEN LAUGHS]

2870
01:57:55,800 --> 01:57:57,567
I'm doing the Memerimar bit.

2871
01:57:57,567 --> 01:58:00,267
Uh, I'm embarrassed to be here.

2872
01:58:00,267 --> 01:58:01,967
I feel like I don't belong here.

2873
01:58:01,967 --> 01:58:03,400
- Your house is so big.
- No, it's okay.

2874
01:58:03,400 --> 01:58:05,633
It's okay.
I'm happy we're here now

2875
01:58:05,633 --> 01:58:09,233
because I had a lot of fun
when we were in Baguio!

2876
01:58:09,233 --> 01:58:10,633
[CROWD LAUGHS]

2877
01:58:10,633 --> 01:58:13,100
[LAUGH TRACK PLAYING]

2878
01:58:13,100 --> 01:58:15,333
[VICE CHUCKLES]

2879
01:58:15,333 --> 01:58:18,500
I didn't know
you'd say it right away.

2880
01:58:18,500 --> 01:58:21,133
- [LAUGHS]
- [LAUGHS, APPLAUSE]

2881
01:58:21,133 --> 01:58:23,200
[CROWD CHEERING]

2882
01:58:23,200 --> 01:58:24,767
I wasn't ready.

2883
01:58:24,767 --> 01:58:27,267
Your house is huge.

2884
01:58:27,300 --> 01:58:29,400
Who else lives here?

2885
01:58:29,400 --> 01:58:32,033
Uh, my mom and I
are the only ones here.

2886
01:58:32,033 --> 01:58:34,600
But your mom
isn't here now, right?

2887
01:58:34,600 --> 01:58:36,033
- [TETAY] Alden?
- Uh, Ma.

2888
01:58:36,033 --> 01:58:39,167
You witch, don't come in yet.
We'll flirt first.

2889
01:58:39,167 --> 01:58:41,900
- I just read this.
- [SILLY SFX PLAYING]

2890
01:58:41,900 --> 01:58:44,267
- Alden?
- I haven't made a move.

2891
01:58:44,267 --> 01:58:45,400
Darn it.

2892
01:58:46,467 --> 01:58:47,467
[TETAY] Please continue.

2893
01:58:47,467 --> 01:58:49,267
You and your mom
are the only ones here?

2894
01:58:49,267 --> 01:58:52,200
- Mm-hmm.
- But now, who's here?

2895
01:58:52,200 --> 01:58:53,433
Uh...

2896
01:58:53,433 --> 01:58:56,600
I think our lawyer is here,

2897
01:58:56,600 --> 01:58:59,500
but my mom and I
are the only ones here.

2898
01:58:59,500 --> 01:59:01,733
But now it's just the two of us.

2899
01:59:01,767 --> 01:59:03,633
Yeah, she went to the salon.

2900
01:59:03,633 --> 01:59:04,933
Oh.

2901
01:59:04,933 --> 01:59:06,467
I think you want us
to do something

2902
01:59:06,467 --> 01:59:07,367
that's why you brought me here.

2903
01:59:07,367 --> 01:59:11,367
Uh, I'm glad we're here now.

2904
01:59:11,367 --> 01:59:14,400
But I miss the times
when you were sweet to me.

2905
01:59:15,000 --> 01:59:19,233
You gave me ube, remember?

2906
01:59:19,233 --> 01:59:21,000
- Where did you buy that?
- Ah, yeah.

2907
01:59:21,000 --> 01:59:24,400
It's specially made.
It's from Good Shepherd.

2908
01:59:24,400 --> 01:59:28,133
There are actually two branches.
One in Tagaytay

2909
01:59:28,133 --> 01:59:29,567
and one in Baguio!

2910
01:59:29,567 --> 01:59:32,333
- [LAUGHTER]
- [SILLY SFX PLAYING]

2911
01:59:33,733 --> 01:59:35,600
- Is it fun there?
- Mm-hmm.

2912
01:59:35,633 --> 01:59:37,767
Why do the people there
seem mad?

2913
01:59:38,567 --> 01:59:40,967
They seem to get mad easily.

2914
01:59:41,933 --> 01:59:45,167
Oh, I'm scared.
I hope someone else arrives

2915
01:59:45,167 --> 01:59:47,933
because you seem to have
anger management issues.

2916
01:59:48,700 --> 01:59:50,167
- Uh...
- [TETAY] Alden!

2917
01:59:50,167 --> 01:59:52,600
- Oh! Who's that?
- Ma. Ma.

2918
01:59:52,600 --> 01:59:54,233
Anger seems to run
in your family.

2919
01:59:54,233 --> 01:59:56,033
- [TETAY GROWLS]
- You're always yelling.

2920
01:59:56,033 --> 01:59:58,400
Alden, you left the door open--
[GASPS]

2921
01:59:58,400 --> 01:59:59,433
Sorry, Ma.

2922
01:59:59,433 --> 02:00:01,800
Where has she been?
Was she out of town?

2923
02:00:02,667 --> 02:00:05,133
She just got home from Baguio!

2924
02:00:05,133 --> 02:00:06,100
[CROWD LAUGHS]

2925
02:00:06,100 --> 02:00:09,233
Uh, I hope you don't
come there again.

2926
02:00:09,267 --> 02:00:10,967
Alden, who's your guest?

2927
02:00:10,967 --> 02:00:13,500
Mom, I'd like you to meet my...

2928
02:00:13,500 --> 02:00:15,200
- Who is that?
- My girlfriend, Mom.

2929
02:00:15,200 --> 02:00:16,967
Where is she?

2930
02:00:16,967 --> 02:00:18,067
Your mom's blind?

2931
02:00:18,067 --> 02:00:19,567
[LAUGHTER]

2932
02:00:19,567 --> 02:00:20,933
Your girl-- [CHUCKLES]

2933
02:00:20,933 --> 02:00:25,233
You told me she's skinny.
Why does she feel fat?

2934
02:00:25,233 --> 02:00:27,333
Your mom seems to be good
at mahjong.

2935
02:00:27,333 --> 02:00:28,467
Mom, that's our couch, Mom.

2936
02:00:29,300 --> 02:00:30,633
- Who is she?
- Mom.

2937
02:00:30,633 --> 02:00:32,533
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

2938
02:00:32,533 --> 02:00:34,267
She's the one
I was telling you about.

2939
02:00:34,267 --> 02:00:35,600
I met her in Baguio!

2940
02:00:35,600 --> 02:00:38,167
[LAUGHTER]

2941
02:00:38,167 --> 02:00:41,200
Every time you shout,
my hairline moves back.

2942
02:00:41,233 --> 02:00:42,267
[LAUGHTER]

2943
02:00:42,267 --> 02:00:44,133
You know...

2944
02:00:44,133 --> 02:00:45,533
are you serious about her?

2945
02:00:46,400 --> 02:00:48,500
That kind of girl,

2946
02:00:48,500 --> 02:00:51,000
the only thing she wants
is our money.

2947
02:00:51,000 --> 02:00:54,067
- Mom, I don't think so, Mom.
- [TETAY] Oh, come on!

2948
02:00:54,067 --> 02:00:55,700
How long have you
been dating her?

2949
02:00:55,700 --> 02:00:57,000
- Three hours, Mom.
- Excuse me.

2950
02:00:57,000 --> 02:00:57,967
Where did you meet her?

2951
02:00:57,967 --> 02:00:58,933
Baguio!

2952
02:00:58,933 --> 02:01:00,067
[LAUGHTER]

2953
02:01:00,067 --> 02:01:01,400
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

2954
02:01:02,367 --> 02:01:04,333
I don't intend
to disrespect you,

2955
02:01:04,333 --> 02:01:07,367
but your mom
is saying hurtful things to me.

2956
02:01:07,367 --> 02:01:10,267
- Look, dear--
- Who really is she?

2957
02:01:10,267 --> 02:01:12,267
- My mom. She's my mom.
- How is she your mom?

2958
02:01:12,267 --> 02:01:13,367
That's Joey Marquez.

2959
02:01:13,367 --> 02:01:15,500
- [LAUGHTER]
- [SILLY SFX PLAYING]

2960
02:01:15,533 --> 02:01:16,633
Son, what's this--

2961
02:01:16,633 --> 02:01:18,733
He used to be a PBA player,
and became an actor.

2962
02:01:18,733 --> 02:01:20,100
How is that your mom?

2963
02:01:20,100 --> 02:01:21,767
Son, your girlfriend is rude!

2964
02:01:21,767 --> 02:01:23,600
Your mom is pretty big.

2965
02:01:23,600 --> 02:01:25,400
I'll spank his mouth,
you'll see!

2966
02:01:25,400 --> 02:01:26,633
[SILLY SFX PLAYING]

2967
02:01:27,900 --> 02:01:29,367
Can't you defend me
from your mom?

2968
02:01:29,367 --> 02:01:31,767
Mom, you motherfather.

2969
02:01:31,767 --> 02:01:32,933
Yes.

2970
02:01:32,933 --> 02:01:35,300
Sometimes I'm a mommy.
Sometimes I'm a father.

2971
02:01:35,300 --> 02:01:36,300
[LAUGHING SFX]

2972
02:01:36,300 --> 02:01:38,367
Why are you like that
to my baby?

2973
02:01:38,367 --> 02:01:40,167
Alden, you just choose.

2974
02:01:40,167 --> 02:01:43,000
If you pick her,
you won't get anything from me,

2975
02:01:43,000 --> 02:01:44,600
not even a cock-eyed cent.

2976
02:01:45,133 --> 02:01:46,433
How did that happen, Mom?

2977
02:01:47,767 --> 02:01:50,167
- That a cent became cock-eyed?
- It went like this.

2978
02:01:50,167 --> 02:01:51,467
[LAUGHTER]

2979
02:01:51,467 --> 02:01:53,233
If you can't defend me,
I'll just leave.

2980
02:01:53,233 --> 02:01:55,033
Wait a minute, don't--
Wait.

2981
02:01:55,033 --> 02:01:56,667
- [VICE GROANS]
- Wow!

2982
02:01:58,067 --> 02:02:02,567
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

2983
02:02:02,567 --> 02:02:04,600
It smells like<i> pansit.
</i>[LAUGHS]

2984
02:02:04,600 --> 02:02:05,867
With ketchup.

2985
02:02:06,600 --> 02:02:09,433
I smelled the<i> pansit
</i>with ketchup.

2986
02:02:10,633 --> 02:02:13,267
But if this is how
our relationship would be...

2987
02:02:14,533 --> 02:02:16,567
It's like I'm in hell.
It's too hot.

2988
02:02:16,567 --> 02:02:19,400
- [TETAY] That's right!
- I want to go someplace cold.

2989
02:02:20,600 --> 02:02:23,233
- Come on. Mom.
- Yes?

2990
02:02:24,067 --> 02:02:25,233
I'm choosing her.

2991
02:02:25,233 --> 02:02:27,100
- Oh my god.
- Don't look for us anymore

2992
02:02:27,100 --> 02:02:28,900
because we're going back
to Baguio!

2993
02:02:29,767 --> 02:02:31,033
[GRUNTING]

2994
02:02:31,033 --> 02:02:32,133
Baguio, Mom!

2995
02:02:37,600 --> 02:02:39,333
[VICE]
You have a bad personality.

2996
02:02:40,167 --> 02:02:41,300
Go to Baguio!

2997
02:02:42,200 --> 02:02:44,333
Look at the attitude
of the person you want to marry.

2998
02:02:44,333 --> 02:02:47,200
You don't even know
her family background.

2999
02:02:47,200 --> 02:02:51,267
She's just a gold digger.
Look at her clothes!

3000
02:02:51,267 --> 02:02:53,400
They're much better than mine.

3001
02:02:54,300 --> 02:02:56,700
- Look. Look!
- So, Mom,

3002
02:02:56,733 --> 02:02:58,800
that's where I'm confused.
Who really is--

3003
02:02:59,600 --> 02:03:01,500
Maybe she can sustain
my lifestyle more than you.

3004
02:03:01,500 --> 02:03:03,567
You want to have a child
with her, Alden?

3005
02:03:03,567 --> 02:03:04,733
Yes, Mom!

3006
02:03:04,733 --> 02:03:06,933
If you really love me,
prove it.

3007
02:03:06,933 --> 02:03:08,833
- Slap your mother.
- [TETAY] Huh?

3008
02:03:09,867 --> 02:03:13,167
Will you slap your mother,
or I will?

3009
02:03:13,167 --> 02:03:14,400
Just slap my mom.

3010
02:03:14,567 --> 02:03:16,000
You've been at it
since earlier.

3011
02:03:16,000 --> 02:03:18,367
You're already hurting
my feelings.

3012
02:03:18,367 --> 02:03:20,867
You're a mom,
but your hands are big.

3013
02:03:20,867 --> 02:03:22,800
My dad played basketball.

3014
02:03:23,400 --> 02:03:26,133
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

3015
02:03:26,133 --> 02:03:27,267
[LAUGHING SFX]

3016
02:03:27,267 --> 02:03:28,267
Oh no.

3017
02:03:29,067 --> 02:03:31,867
I won't let you keep treating me
this way.

3018
02:03:31,867 --> 02:03:34,433
- You don't know me.
- I know you.

3019
02:03:35,200 --> 02:03:36,667
You don't know me.

3020
02:03:36,667 --> 02:03:38,533
You're a low-class person, dear.

3021
02:03:38,533 --> 02:03:40,567
[AUDIENCE LAUGHING]

3022
02:03:40,567 --> 02:03:44,633
You're the kind of woman
who's only after our money!

3023
02:03:45,833 --> 02:03:48,200
Those clothes you wear
as if you're--

3024
02:03:48,567 --> 02:03:50,567
I will not allow myself
to be treated like this.

3025
02:03:53,067 --> 02:03:56,333
- It's time you meet her.
- Huh? Who?

3026
02:03:58,067 --> 02:04:00,167
I won't let your mother
belittle me,

3027
02:04:00,167 --> 02:04:02,967
- so I brought our attorney.
- Okay.

3028
02:04:03,000 --> 02:04:04,700
- Attorney.
- This is the attorney.

3029
02:04:04,700 --> 02:04:06,567
She's Atty.<i> Kaponyan
</i>(she's neutered).

3030
02:04:07,267 --> 02:04:08,400
- [ALDEN]<i> Kaponyan?
</i>- What's her name?

3031
02:04:08,400 --> 02:04:10,200
- [VICE]<i> Kaponyan.
</i>- Am I a dog?

3032
02:04:10,200 --> 02:04:12,067
Yes, you're an<i> aboga-dog
</i>(attorney dog).

3033
02:04:12,900 --> 02:04:14,233
She's Atty. Kaponyan.

3034
02:04:15,100 --> 02:04:16,467
- Why--
- She's belittling me.

3035
02:04:16,467 --> 02:04:18,033
- Why--
- Love, come here, love!

3036
02:04:19,700 --> 02:04:22,500
Why are you belittling
my client?

3037
02:04:22,500 --> 02:04:26,100
Stop it. I'll get a jar,
and put you inside.

3038
02:04:26,100 --> 02:04:29,867
Didn't you know she's an heiress
of the Sterling family?

3039
02:04:29,867 --> 02:04:32,900
Wow. I knew it.
I knew it.

3040
02:04:32,900 --> 02:04:35,500
She came from a wealthy family!

3041
02:04:35,533 --> 02:04:37,900
- [TETAY] What?!
- And that's not all.

3042
02:04:37,900 --> 02:04:42,733
She's very intelligent.
She scored 719 in her math exam!

3043
02:04:42,733 --> 02:04:44,300
Wow, I knew it.

3044
02:04:44,300 --> 02:04:46,467
I am Linda Runner.

3045
02:04:46,467 --> 02:04:49,867
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

3046
02:04:49,867 --> 02:04:51,800
- [ALDEN] That's Mom's favorite.
- [TETAY] Is it true?

3047
02:04:52,600 --> 02:04:54,100
Is what you are saying all true?

3048
02:04:54,767 --> 02:04:55,767
Yes!

3049
02:04:56,800 --> 02:04:59,600
Therefore, you have no right
to belittle her!

3050
02:04:59,600 --> 02:05:02,133
Don't yell at my mother!

3051
02:05:02,133 --> 02:05:04,667
Therefore, you have no right
to belittle her! Oh.

3052
02:05:04,667 --> 02:05:06,233
I'm your client!

3053
02:05:07,500 --> 02:05:10,400
Therefore, you have no right
to belittle her!

3054
02:05:10,433 --> 02:05:11,867
Don't you remember her?

3055
02:05:12,567 --> 02:05:14,867
- Babe. Who is--
- We bought her.

3056
02:05:14,867 --> 02:05:17,567
She's the ashtray.
She had a round thing.

3057
02:05:17,567 --> 02:05:19,333
We bought her from--
Where did we go again?

3058
02:05:19,333 --> 02:05:20,867
- The one that goes like this?
- Yes!

3059
02:05:20,867 --> 02:05:22,300
- And then this comes out?
- Yes!

3060
02:05:22,300 --> 02:05:23,367
- In Baguio!
- Ah!

3061
02:05:25,367 --> 02:05:26,333
In Bag--

3062
02:05:27,133 --> 02:05:28,667
- There.
- Sorry.

3063
02:05:28,667 --> 02:05:30,100
- Don't hurt her.
- The relationships

3064
02:05:30,100 --> 02:05:31,600
- are confusing me.
- Wait!

3065
02:05:31,600 --> 02:05:33,400
I want you to know...

3066
02:05:34,767 --> 02:05:36,800
Ever since you lost
your mother...

3067
02:05:37,633 --> 02:05:40,900
Attorney and I got closer.

3068
02:05:40,900 --> 02:05:44,767
Wow, your mom flirts
with a spider inside a matchbox.

3069
02:05:44,800 --> 02:05:47,533
[LAUGHING SFX]

3070
02:05:47,533 --> 02:05:51,233
Please forgive me.
I didn't mean to...

3071
02:05:51,933 --> 02:05:54,933
- ...say those things to you.
- [VICE] Don't worry.

3072
02:05:55,500 --> 02:05:57,300
- They're being possessed.
- My parents taught me

3073
02:05:57,300 --> 02:05:59,867
not to fight with the elderly.

3074
02:05:59,867 --> 02:06:01,500
- Wow.
- And I shouldn't harbor

3075
02:06:01,500 --> 02:06:04,033
resentment and anger
towards anyone.

3076
02:06:04,033 --> 02:06:07,100
I love your son.
And I forgive you.

3077
02:06:07,100 --> 02:06:08,733
Thank you very much.

3078
02:06:08,733 --> 02:06:10,600
You won't hear anything bad
from me.

3079
02:06:10,600 --> 02:06:13,300
- But I know you move fast.
- No.

3080
02:06:14,233 --> 02:06:17,500
I've known you
for more than two decades.

3081
02:06:18,367 --> 02:06:20,667
- I forgive you.
- Thank you.

3082
02:06:20,667 --> 02:06:22,367
- I'm a good person.
- Thank you.

3083
02:06:22,367 --> 02:06:24,400
And I won't ever do something
ill towards you.

3084
02:06:24,400 --> 02:06:25,567
Thank you, Sarah.

3085
02:06:27,333 --> 02:06:28,433
Please forgive me.

3086
02:06:29,267 --> 02:06:30,533
I love your mother more.

3087
02:06:30,533 --> 02:06:31,767
[AUDIENCE LAUGHS, SCREAMS]

3088
02:06:31,767 --> 02:06:34,700
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

3089
02:06:34,700 --> 02:06:38,067
Let's give a round of applause
to Alden!

3090
02:06:38,067 --> 02:06:39,967
- [ALDEN] Woo!
- Yay!

3091
02:06:39,967 --> 02:06:41,400
[VICE]
Alden, thank you very much.

3092
02:06:41,400 --> 02:06:44,500
I had so, so, so, so,
so much fun tonight!

3093
02:06:44,500 --> 02:06:46,267
It is, um...

3094
02:06:46,267 --> 02:06:48,167
It was more
than what I expected,

3095
02:06:48,200 --> 02:06:49,567
to tell you honestly, Vice.

3096
02:06:49,567 --> 02:06:52,667
To the entire creatives team,
thank you for having me here.

3097
02:06:53,733 --> 02:06:55,767
This is now my core memory.

3098
02:06:55,767 --> 02:06:57,467
This is very life-changing
for me.

3099
02:06:57,467 --> 02:07:01,700
One of the highlights,
not of 2026, but my life.

3100
02:07:02,667 --> 02:07:04,933
I would like to consider
this opportunity--

3101
02:07:04,933 --> 02:07:07,833
I'm not exaggerating here.

3102
02:07:07,833 --> 02:07:11,300
But I had a lot of moments,

3103
02:07:11,300 --> 02:07:13,700
so I feel very blessed
to be here.

3104
02:07:13,700 --> 02:07:14,800
Thank you very much.

3105
02:07:14,800 --> 02:07:18,100
I am just so happy
to see you enjoying yourself,

3106
02:07:18,100 --> 02:07:20,367
the set, us, and everyone,

3107
02:07:20,367 --> 02:07:24,500
and just being yourself,
and having so much fun.

3108
02:07:24,533 --> 02:07:26,333
I always see you ever since.

3109
02:07:26,333 --> 02:07:28,967
I watch you, I admire you.

3110
02:07:28,967 --> 02:07:30,733
I find you handsome,
I find you kind.

3111
02:07:30,733 --> 02:07:32,867
But your personality
is just so colorful!

3112
02:07:32,867 --> 02:07:37,433
There's still so much
we don't know about you.

3113
02:07:37,433 --> 02:07:41,000
And when we see you,
you're so happy.

3114
02:07:41,000 --> 02:07:43,600
Your aura feels so light.

3115
02:07:43,600 --> 02:07:47,033
And I hope that many people
around the world can see

3116
02:07:47,033 --> 02:07:51,800
that Alden is more than just a
pretty face and a talented guy.

3117
02:07:51,800 --> 02:07:55,733
- [TETAY] True.
- He's a guy--

3118
02:07:55,767 --> 02:08:00,567
He's an ordinary guy,
and yet he's special.

3119
02:08:00,567 --> 02:08:02,733
But he's just like us.

3120
02:08:02,733 --> 02:08:06,933
He feels a lot, he does a lot,
he fools around a lot,

3121
02:08:06,933 --> 02:08:08,667
he has a lot...

3122
02:08:10,267 --> 02:08:12,800
He has a lot of strengths
and weaknesses.

3123
02:08:12,800 --> 02:08:18,933
He has a lot of imperfections,
but still, he's very special.

3124
02:08:19,900 --> 02:08:21,500
And thank you so much
for treating

3125
02:08:21,500 --> 02:08:23,033
this program very special

3126
02:08:23,033 --> 02:08:25,100
because you did a lot of things
we only saw

3127
02:08:25,100 --> 02:08:27,033
- you do for the first time.
- Yes, a lot!

3128
02:08:27,033 --> 02:08:28,433
And stories you told
for the first time.

3129
02:08:28,467 --> 02:08:31,200
It's the first time I danced...

3130
02:08:32,000 --> 02:08:34,000
...in front of a
very beautiful<i> dilag</i> (woman).

3131
02:08:34,000 --> 02:08:35,133
[CHUCKLING]

3132
02:08:35,133 --> 02:08:36,833
- That's nothing.
<i> - Dalag</i> (mudfish), sorry.

3133
02:08:36,833 --> 02:08:38,400
I meant a very beautiful dalag.

3134
02:08:38,400 --> 02:08:39,867
<i> - Dalag.
</i>- A very beautiful dalag.

3135
02:08:39,867 --> 02:08:41,900
- We're hard to catch.
- [ALDEN LAUGHS]

3136
02:08:41,900 --> 02:08:42,867
We're quite slippery.

3137
02:08:42,867 --> 02:08:44,500
- Sorry.
- But thank you.

3138
02:08:44,500 --> 02:08:45,667
We appreciate you.

3139
02:08:45,667 --> 02:08:49,200
We're glad that you're our guest
for our first episode!

3140
02:08:49,200 --> 02:08:50,267
[CHEERING]

3141
02:08:50,267 --> 02:08:51,333
We did it!

3142
02:08:51,333 --> 02:08:56,733
We did it!
Our first episode of<i> GGV</i> on GMA!

3143
02:08:56,733 --> 02:08:58,533
Certified fresh.

3144
02:08:58,533 --> 02:09:01,300
Fresh episode, fresh guest,

3145
02:09:01,300 --> 02:09:04,733
fresh stories, fresh fun
and everything under the sun.

3146
02:09:04,767 --> 02:09:07,100
Thank you so much,
Alden Richards!

3147
02:09:07,100 --> 02:09:08,233
Thank you, Vice.

3148
02:09:08,233 --> 02:09:10,800
Thank you to everyone
behind Gandang Gabi, Vice!

3149
02:09:10,800 --> 02:09:13,933
Thank you as well to
our<i> Kapamilyas</i> and Kapusos

3150
02:09:13,933 --> 02:09:15,467
who watched the pilot episode.

3151
02:09:15,467 --> 02:09:16,633
Thank you so much.

3152
02:09:16,633 --> 02:09:18,433
Thank you.
What's your new show?

3153
02:09:18,433 --> 02:09:19,600
- You're shooting it now, right?
- Oh!

3154
02:09:19,600 --> 02:09:23,100
Please watch out for
<i> Love, Siargao,</i>

3155
02:09:23,100 --> 02:09:24,400
a Viu Original series.

3156
02:09:24,400 --> 02:09:26,967
It will air on September 28,

3157
02:09:26,967 --> 02:09:29,767
Monday to Friday, at 9:35 PM

3158
02:09:29,767 --> 02:09:31,067
